(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ev-8"] = {"561001101":[["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","Nothing at all."],["","My consciousness seems to have returned, but from the outside world—nothing."],["","Opening my eyes, all I see is darkness."],["","Listening closely, only silence."],["","...Who am I?"],["","Where am I?"],["","What can I do?"],["","I'm not sure if having only consciousness without these answers constitutes existence."],["","So to find out, I reach out and feel myself..."],["","Then, memories begin to emerge."],["","My existence starts to become real."],["","We still have a chance... Stay alert, Sylvie! Hurry, break through and get out of here!"],["","What are you saying, Rosa...? You can't do this alone!"],["","You know, the UNCS would never give up on \"Diaz\"..."],["","Quickly, take them both away... and then stop others from becoming sacrifices to these nightmares!"],["","Sylvie, I know you can do all this."],["","..."],["","After that, Sylvie... did you manage to escape with Hong and Emily?"],["","..."],["","It's all my fault. If I had acted faster, the alarm wouldn't have been triggered... and you wouldn't have to bear this burden..."],["","Compared to you, I'm the incompetent sister."],["","We just need two more days... Our dream's in reach—"],["","Ha... How many chances did we miss, letting the NDF run wild?"],["","One person can't change Milkhama's fate. It's destined as the powers' battleground!"],["","I won't be alone... After me, Milkhama's people will rise up..."],["","No more empty words... What happened to my sisters..."],["","It ends now."],["","..."],["","Just how far ahead had Goman planned... just as he said, what I saw as an opportunity ultimately led to more sacrifices."],["","And those who escaped, without anyone to provide them shelter, didn't know how long they could hide."],["","If only I had thought it through more carefully... like when I sent Ada away, following Goman's plan..."],["","..."],["","No... I simply lost to my own regret."],["","So, you've finally decided to show yourself. Listen, Kaidan—this isn't the time for doubt. Take your team and run as far as you can."],["","What, you want me to run like a coward again?"],["","No, just looking out for your team's safety, that's all. Besides, my fight here... it's personal."],["","...!?"],["","Got it... Let's move! Rosa, we'll regroup outside White Maple!"],["","..."],["","Sorry... Kaidan, I couldn't fulfill any of the promises I made to you."],["","Someone as untrustworthy as me, still begging your forgiveness at the very end... How shameless..."],["","..."],["","But if I'd held on just a little longer, everything would've been different."],["","That's right... if only I'd been stronger..."],["","Memories like fragments keep surfacing, but I no longer need to piece them together."],["","I know who I am."],["","..."],["Rosa","I am Rosa Diaz."],["Rosa","The prototype of the Hyper-Aptamer Project, the source of all tragedies."],["Rosa","The Valkyrie of the UNCS, the beginning of all slaughter."],["Rosa","My battle is not over yet."]],"561001301":[["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","Failed again."],["","..."],["","Not enough... this level, it's just not enough..."],["","I was too weak back then... I should've realized that power, no matter what form it took, was not something I was in a position to refuse..."],["","Must... must get stronger... to protect them..."],["","Sylvie, block her!"],["","...!?"],["","This voice is..."],["","On it... My turn to save you, sis!"],["","Uh... Sister? Are you talking about me?"],["","Valkyrie in the flesh... Let's see if you live up to the hype."],["","Why... can't see anything..."],["","You'll be essential to my strength, fighting alongside me to crush those shortsighted insects..."],["","These people are... no..."],["","What am I... now..."],["","Incredible! The Valkyrie's awake!"],["","Really now... then tell me, who is Sylvie? Who is Kaidan Newman?"],["","We found her! It's Rosa!"],["","Voices... More and more voices..."],["","Stop... Stop now!"],["","Damn, those Predator monsters!"],["","Thanks for your assistance, GKD Parcel Service, and of course, our dear \"Miss Inspector\"!"],["","It's working, Kaidan! ST's back under our control!"],["","You guys are totally dropping the ball! Can't handle one single woman?"],["","No way are we losing you again!"],["","No one's leaving today."],["","What did you do to Rosa!?"],["","..."],["","No... I can't run away from all this... I must save everyone..."],["","If this is the cost, I have no choice..."],["","I must continue fighting... until..."],["","..."],["","...When?"],["","This obsession... Indeed, the real you has never changed..."],["Rosa","Who are you? How did you find this place...?"],["","...Even if you have forgotten everything, it doesn't matter."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","No... your name is..."],["","I'm here to take you home, sis."],["Rosa","Ada!!!!!!"],["","With a hurried and feeble call, Rosa awoke from an operating table."],["","This nightmare that had dragged on and on—it ended with a call."],["Rosa","...Hmm..."],["","Surprise, guilt, confusion—the flood of emotions finally caught up with her as a dull throb pulsed through the back of her skull, forcing her to squeeze her eyes shut and groan, clutching her head."],["","The chaotic, wordless voices still echoed, as if they were trying to shatter her consciousness, rampaging through her mind."],["Rosa","What... what happened?"],["","After a while, the storm in her mind settled, and Rosa was finally able to get up and observe her surroundings."],["","Another operating room in a research institute. She's seen her share."],["Rosa","This isn't a Hyper-Aptamer, not even a UNCS research institute..."],["","The precision instruments everywhere <yellow>bear no faction markings</yellow>. After some searching, there's no more useful information, only some documents recording her body parameters."],["","\"Purification surgery successful... Vital signs stable... Expected to awaken from coma <yellow>soon</yellow>...\""],["","But she quickly noticed that only <yellow>a small portion of the medications in some cabinets showed signs of use</yellow>, indicating that she hadn't been transferred to this operating room for too long."],["","She reasoned that not much time had passed since that battle."],["Rosa","Wasn't I recovered by the UNCS...? And there's not a single person here... What is this place...?"],["","It's quite remarkable that people may not know how a dream begins, but they can always clearly understand how it ends."],["","Regarding reality, the last fragment of Rosa's memory is the fireworks licking the night sky in White Maple, followed by that long, now gradually fading nightmare."],["Rosa","First, I need to get out of here. Then I need to contact Sylvie and the others... and that merc too..."],["","After making up her mind, Rosa endured the pain and began searching for something to replace her inconvenient hospital gown, eventually finding a pitch-black combat suit in a corner junk box."],["","It looks like a perfect fit and might be the best choice for the upcoming action, but the moment Rosa reached out to touch the outfit, she abandoned the idea."],["","For some reason, this combat suit emitted a repulsive aura."],["","As if it were the nightmare itself."]],"561002101":[["","Base Surveillance Room"],["","A smart and capable girl is scanning the dozens of softly glowing screens—<yellow>the numerous hidden cameras placed throughout the base</yellow> capture everything happening within the facility."],["","She had been half-asleep, eyes drooping, when a brief electric jolt from the device snapped her awake—she scrambled frantically for the microphone beside her and called out."],["???","E-Everyone! The surgery was a success! Rosa's awake!"],["","The first to arrive was a flash of pink—she grabbed the nearest wheeled chair, dropped into it and, with a kick, went careening across the room like she was riding into battle."],["","Bang!"],["","The girl originally responsible for monitoring was bumped aside along with her chair."],["???","...Ah! Paloma, don't move around!"],["Paloma","Huh? Strange... She's not wearing that combat suit? Doesn't she know how much trouble it is for me to clean it myself without sending it to the laundry?"],["","Ignoring the girl's loud complaints beside her, Paloma frowned as she operated the equipment, zooming in on Rosa's figure and recording her frozen expression when she touched the combat suit."],["Paloma","She doesn't even smell it. I bet there's not a trace of scent left... Hey, Sapientia, what do you think is the reason?"],["","Paloma asked the girl beside her earnestly."],["Sapientia","I... I don't know about that... Just move aside, I need to track Rosa's movements!"],["Paloma","I won't move unless you answer."],["Sapientia","Has she maybe... gone off that style of combat suit?"],["Paloma","...Sapi, are you an idiot?"],["","Paloma glanced at Sapientia, even though she was the one who started talking nonsense first."],["Paloma","This doesn't fit the <yellow>Predator</yellow>'s mindset at all. You can't exactly pilot an ST in a hospital gown. All that equipment would rub her raw..."],["???","If she can remember what she went through, it's only natural for her to reject that gear."],["","At some point, a burly man had appeared behind them, casting a shadow over the console."],["Sapientia","Great, the Vice Captain is finally here..."],["","Sapientia let out a long sigh. It was just like when children are fighting, and the more sensible side finally has an adult to uphold justice."],["","But Paloma thought otherwise—she had always been the troublemaker of the group, and no matter how dependable an adult was, they could never quite win her over. If anything, it just made her play it straight-faced."],["Paloma","...Leopold, you do remember everything I spent that whole afternoon explaining to you, right?"],["Paloma","There might be some unexpected events... but she'll never, ever, ever escape the effects of those experiments. It's like paper burned to ashes that can't be restored; the process is irreversible."],["Paloma","If it were really that simple to overcome everything, wouldn't all my research up to now be nothing but a joke?"],["Leopold","Of course I haven't forgotten, but I also understand that if it weren't for that slight possibility, you wouldn't have agreed to Ada's plan, right?"],["Paloma","..."],["","Paloma stubbornly stared at Leopold for a while, as if even her prosthetic eye was straining, but facing that eternally calm face, she realized it was just a futile effort."],["","Kicking the chair to the side, she returned the console's position to Sapientia, crossed her arms, and circled around the conference room following the momentum of the chair."],["Paloma","Fine, I won't argue with you. Just don't blame me for not warning you when she gets on that modified XR-Plutone, <yellow>Erinys</yellow>."],["Paloma","Then I'll report to Captain Ada fiercely, plus the credit for finding the \"Legacy\" earlier... Hehe... Looks like Sapi will soon be demoted to be my intern..."],["Leopold","..."],["Paloma","Huh? Why is no one talking? C'mon, gimme something..."],["Sapientia","Why did she actually <yellow>give up</yellow>..."],["","The moment she heard the word \"give up,\" Paloma stopped spinning and looked at the surveillance screen."],["","Rosa had already arrived at the facility's hangar. In front of the Erinys, at once both familiar and strange, she only paused briefly before deciding to leave."],["","Everyone present understood what this meant, but each derived a different meaning from it."],["","Paloma's smile froze; just now, her so-called law was easily shattered by Rosa."],["Leopold","Ada, it may have already become reality..."],["","A hint of a smile flashed across Leopold's stone-hard features, then disappeared as he settled back into his customary calm."],["Leopold","Sapientia, are all the STs ready for deployment?"],["Sapientia","Yes, but those barriers at the base entrance are still..."],["Leopold","It's not often you get the chance to face that Valkyrie from the UNCS head-on, so taking a few risks at a time like this is understandable."],["Leopold","Everyone, don't have any regrets..."],["","As Leopold issued instructions to the crowd and turned to open the two heavy doors, a tardy guest happened to bump into his broad chest."],["","Looking up, he saw Leopold's slightly furrowed brow."],["???","..."],["Leopold","..."],["???","Sorry, I'm a bit late... What are we supposed to do now?"],["Paloma","Don't just stand there, we're going after Rosa!"],["","Paloma squeezed through the gap between Leopold and the door, and hurriedly ran down the corridor."],["Paloma","Sloth, next time you're late, let me know. It's been a while since I've seen the Vice Captain lose his temper!"],["","She had already recovered from the brief shock earlier and was eager to witness it all firsthand."],["","Paloma has always been hands-on."],["Sloth","Uh, sure. If I remember..."]],"561002301":[["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Hmm..."],["","Rosa wakes up, still disoriented, instinctively reaching out to shield herself from the familiar and glaring light."],["","The figure beside the operating table leaned forward, his broad arms completing the task for her, casting a shadow."],["Leopold","You awake?"],["Rosa","You are..."],["","Rosa propped herself up, her weakness beyond her imagination, and her exhausted arms slipped on the table, causing her to fall face down."],["","The people around her wanted to step forward to support her, but Rosa's hand slapped on the table, steadying herself."],["","Even though she was already a fish on the chopping block, she remained vigilant."],["Leopold","Leopold Ashford, just call me Leopold."],["Paloma","It's best not to move around. Your body probably isn't under your brain's control right now, so give it some time to recover."],["","Another grinning face leaned in, and a familiar voice reawakened the memories she had lost due to the pain."],["Rosa","...Paloma?"],["Paloma","Wow, I'm touched! You remembered my name after hearing it just once?"],["Paloma","I definitely couldn't do that. Even my teammates who are with me every day... Hey, what's your name again?"],["Sapientia","It's Sapientia! Sapientia!"],["","Following the direction Paloma pointed, another figure darted out from the side and started bickering with her."],["","Rosa is like a delicacy at a banquet, with diners on both sides waiting to savor her."],["Rosa","Who are you... really...?"],["Leopold","...Alright, all of you move aside a bit. Behave yourselves like Sloth."],["Leopold","Let's <yellow>speed things up</yellow> and wrap up this simple meeting... There's more to do later."],["","Under Leopold's instructions, the lively scene finally quieted down, and Rosa noticed the fourth person in the corner of the operating room, with their head lowered."],["","The one who arrived at the battlefield at the last moment and dealt her the fatal blow."],["Sloth","..."],["Sloth","Huff... Huff..."],["","No matter how you look at it, the reason he didn't join this farce was simply because he was dozing off."],["Leopold","Before answering your question, you must first answer the question I asked during the battle."],["Leopold","At that time, you already knew the answer in your heart."],["","\"Rather than that, I want to know which faction you think we belong to...\""],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","You are with Obsidian, aren't you?"],["","UNCS is the absolute leader in Hyper-Aptamer experiment, but beyond that, it also has intricate connections with the pharmaceutical company named Obsidian."],["","While planning the uprising, Rosa considered the possible influence of Obsidian, but ultimately the only enemy she could identify was Blair."],["","After all, they knew nothing about the real Obsidian."],["Leopold","So that's your answer... Very well..."],["","Leopold showed a relieved smile, it seems Rosa's answer satisfied him greatly, enough to let him put down the last bit of guard."],["Leopold","We are..."],["Sloth","Sloth, Reversion Squad, under the DL Oceanic Conclave."],["","A voice from the corner interrupted Leopold's words, he yawned and looked at everyone, seemingly unaware of what mistake he just made."],["Paloma","Ah, Sloth stole the Vice Captain's lines."],["Sloth","Just took a nap... What's going on? Weren't we supposed to introduce ourselves when Rosa woke up?"],["Rosa","You are from the DL, how is this possible... Could it be..."],["","Ignoring Sloth's sudden interruption, an undeniable possibility has already formed in Rosa's mind."],["Leopold","That's right, Ada sent us."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","So, was that dream real?"],["","Rosa asked incredulously, as the joy, guilt, and emotion brought by that call were once again awakened, becoming incredibly vivid."],["Leopold","That's the reality. Your sister, Ada Diaz, is now the hope for the future of the alliance and the captain of our Reversion Squad..."],["Rosa","Then... where is she now?! Please tell me, I thought I'd never see..."],["","Chaotic emotions boil within, and a faint flush appears on Rosa's pale face as she eagerly questions the previous enemy."],["","Coma in White Maple? Unknown sensory abilities? Imprisoned by the DL? The mysteries are innumerable, but at this moment, she has no heart to pursue them further."],["","Ada... Rosa had given up hope of seeing her again..."],["Leopold","I understand your desire to see her, but given your status, going to the DL's core... You must understand that the DL has not officially acknowledged your containment; everything is under Ada's personal directive."],["","Those in high positions often have burdens that bind their hands; the Rosa of the past understood this best."],["Rosa","If possible, even a remote conversation would..."],["Leopold","Unfortunately, she is currently busy with the <yellow>Legacy</yellow> matter, and no one can contact her for a while."],["Rosa","Legacy again... Sorry, I only remember my battle with Blair in White Maple... Did you take me away at that time?"],["","Another unfamiliar term, Rosa racks her brain to recall the past, but every effort touches that nightmare like a quagmire."],["","And from that nightmare, all she can gain is pain."],["Paloma","Oh no, you're not really going to start from that time, are you?"],["Paloma","Sloth, you can go back to sleep. What's coming next is as boring as those recap episodes in anime."],["Sloth","..."],["","When no one paid attention to him, he had already closed his eyes again."],["Leopold","Sapientia, is all the relevant information prepared?"],["Sapientia","Yes, I've organized it into a more readable format."],["","Sapientia stood up and handed an operation screen to Rosa. As her fingertips glided, countless images and texts racked before her."],["","This information can help her recognize what has happened in the past, but in fact, she already knows, she just doesn't want to admit it..."],["","That nightmare is the past."]],"561003101":[["Rosa","..."],["","After a long silence, Rosa closed the final segment of footage and returned the control screen to the somewhat uneasy Sapientia."],["","These images recorded everything that happened during the coma phase, which also explains how Paloma was able to recount the scene at that time."],["","Unlike the past, Milkhama can no longer hide new secrets."],["Sapientia","I'm sorry you had to hear that—it's not a pretty past..."],["Rosa","Did I really do this...?"],["","Former enemies met an abrupt demise, and friends found calm paths and new struggles—but..."],["","The nightmares she experienced were real."],["","She once pointed her weapon at a comrade."],["Paloma","There's nothing to blame yourself for!"],["","Even the eccentric one chimed in to encourage her."],["Paloma","Your straightforward partners will surely forgive you, and legally, if certain conditions are met, some mentally ill individuals are not subject to criminal penalties but are sent for treatment first, right?"],["Paloma","So regardless of how you look at it, redemption is within your reach!"],["Rosa","But if I had woken earlier..."],["Paloma","Pointless."],["Leopold","Enough, Paloma."],["","Leopold spoke up to try to stop Paloma, but it was to no avail... or perhaps he understood that Paloma would reveal the whole truth regardless."],["Paloma","Although you are indeed that <yellow>Perfect Hyper-Aptamer</yellow>, in the end, humans are still humans..."],["Paloma","On your own, you cannot defeat the arashi matter."],["Rosa","...What?"],["Paloma","Have you ever wondered why you suddenly woke up from the Renovation?"],["Paloma","Though it was rushed, Obsidian really did use the Rebirth technology on you back then... Ah, that tech—maybe it's time for a little refresher in case anyone's forgotten."],["Paloma","Simply put, it's a technology that injects arashi matter into the human body, allowing it to fuse with cells, thereby increasing the affinity between humans and STs, with the side effect of messing up the brain."],["Paloma","I know, you can recall the feelings at that time. Was it really an obstacle overcome by sheer willpower?"],["Rosa","..."],["","Rosa wanted to argue, but as someone involved, she knew it wasn't a dream you could wake up from by pinching your cheeks, nor a dreamscape that could be shattered by a companion's call."],["","According to Paloma's words, Ada's final call was not the key either."],["","Those modifications have completely twisted her soul."],["Rosa","Sorry, please tell..."],["Sapientia","It's the PAMS System. Nanobots equipped with it monitor the dynamic distribution of arashi material in your body in real-time and analyze the corresponding biometric identification... Hmm... It's like targeted therapy..."],["Paloma","Hey—Sapi, how could you just give her the answer like that? That's just..."],["","This time, Leopold placed his hand on Paloma's shoulder and shook his head, finally quieting the noisy girl for a moment."],["","If it's meant as a lesson, she has already crossed the line; going further would just become ridicule."],["","This time, she obediently handed the stage over to her teammates."],["Sapientia","I think Paloma has her reasons for giving you a hard time. She's not used to leaving a good impression on others, but in reality..."],["Sapientia","She proposed and primarily executed this treatment plan. I only helped a bit with the robot's design."],["","Sapientia deliberately lowered her voice to tell Rosa this little secret."],["","A simple fact made Rosa greatly change her view of the annoying one."],["Sapientia","But with our current technology, we can only complete the inspection task. The remaining suppression and inactivation processes..."],["Rosa","Wait a minute."],["","Rosa suddenly interrupted Sapientia's statement with a soft voice, making a shushing gesture."],["","Her gaze passed over everyone present and looked at the empty doorway."],["","Her meaning was clear, there was a sixth person outside the door who was not present."],["???","...I'm really surprised, when did you notice?"],["","A tall woman stepped into the operating room; her attire put Rosa on guard."],["","Without any concealment, the emblem representing Obsidian was displayed prominently on her chest."],["Rosa","Everyone, this one's been..."],["","She was about to alert her companions, but Rosa soon understood that, apart from her, the others held only a bit of discomfort toward the unexpected visitor, not a trace of real malice."],["???","You guessed it right, I've been standing outside the door for two minutes, just waiting for you to call me in."],["","The woman unabashedly surveyed the room and found a suitable place to sit, just as if she belonged there."],["Morgana","I'm Morgana, and since I'm in a bit of a hurry, I'll keep it brief... Didn't that Sapi just say that DL couldn't find a way to deactivate the arashi material inside you? But we have to find a way to save you, right?"],["Rosa","Are you..."],["","Rosa was somewhat incredulous. She looked at Leopold, recalling her previous conversation with him."],["","He did not <yellow>deny</yellow> her accusation regarding the Obsidian."],["Leopold","To save you, we have no choice."],["Rosa","No... I can't let Ada go that far just for me..."],["Morgana","Alright, alright—can you let me finish? The bit where you cry and wail \"how could you possibly team up with that damn Obsidian just for my sake\"—we aren't there yet!"],["Morgana","This kind of drama has already been played by Epiphyllum before, just replacing UNCS with Obsidian, and everyone is definitely tired of it!"],["","Morgana clapped her hands to interrupt Rosa's accusations, laughing and playing with everyone's nerves with facts."],["","Everyone remains silent, perhaps something happened earlier that forced them to accept this fact."],["","But there is one person who refuses to accept it."],["Rosa","Shut up! How could A... Ada..."],["Leopold","Calm down first, this is also for..."],["","Rosa suppresses her physical discomfort and angrily shouts at Morgana."],["Morgana","What a hassle... How about this, let's make a trade."],["Morgana","I can answer one question unconditionally, and then you have to listen to the rest of what I have to say, deal?"],["","An incredibly tempting and fair condition that calmed the anxious Valkyrie."],["Rosa","...What do you want to use Ada for?"],["Morgana","Well... Sorry, I don't know! Okay, now it's my turn to speak..."],["Rosa","You've got to be joking!?"],["Morgana","If I don't know something, then I just don't know. I'm just middle management, following orders from above... But soon the president will meet Ada, and then both sides will know the details of the Trade..."],["Morgana","Right now, I can only tell you one thing—I have received orders to <yellow>unconditionally assist the Reversion Squad</yellow>, and that's it."],["","A shrewd character like her wouldn't tell such a clumsy lie... So, it must be the truth."],["","Rosa accepted this fact, at least for now, Morgana in front of her was not an enemy."],["Rosa","..."],["Morgana","Finally, things have calmed down... The treatment is not over yet. We have only <yellow>suppressed</yellow> your abilities and symptoms with the most brutal formula."],["Morgana","Even within the group, this was an unprecedented attempt. No one knew what the situation would be before you woke up."],["","So every member of the previous team was probing Rosa, trying to find out if she had returned to normal and whether she was still under Obsidian's control..."],["Morgana","But the result is good. Not only have you broken free from the brainwashing, but you also seem to have the ability to sense other <yellow>Predators</yellow>..."],["Paloma","Not just Predators, perhaps everyone who has undergone the <yellow>arashi matter implant surgery</yellow> is within her perception range."],["","Paloma stepped forward to point out Morgana's oversight, shifting from her previous playful demeanor to a serious tone, as if she were the attending physician Sapientia often mentioned, in the black-and-white realm of scientific observation."],["Paloma","Rosa, earlier in the battle, you did sense Sloth's presence, didn't you?"],["Rosa","...That's right."],["","There are a total of four enemies, and before Sloth appeared, Rosa had already vaguely sensed his presence."],["","Apart from everything that can be perceived by normal senses, Rosa has gradually understood what they mean by <yellow>sensing</yellow>."],["","Even now, with eyes closed and ears covered, in that void of darkness and silence, Rosa can still sense the five people around her, standing out like beacons in the night."],["","And she is also certain that she can distinguish between the four and Morgana. Compared to the former, Morgana brings a more chaotic and cold feeling."],["Morgana","Oh? Is that so... That is truly an unexpected gain..."],["Morgana","I originally thought this phenomenon only occurred among Predators. It seems the database needs an update."],["","Morgana looked at Paloma with great interest. Before this, she seemed to have never looked directly at her."],["Morgana","Paloma, right? Are you interested in <yellow>returning</yellow> to work at Obsidian?"],["Morgana","Of course, I don't mean at headquarters. The president here can give you a much better deal... Even an immersive laboratory like this, built with masses of <yellow>arashi matter constructs</yellow>—it wouldn't be out of the question."],["Morgana","The rewards here are much better than you can imagine."],["Paloma","Ah, is this called re-employment? That indeed requires higher compensation for me to..."],["Sapientia","Don't... don't even think about it. She's long been unrelated to Obsidian!"],["","Sapientia stood between the two, striving to make her voice more fearless, and sternly rejected Morgana's invitation."],["Paloma","Ah... I'm sorry, just as Sapi said, I really don't quite fit with your corporate spirit."],["Paloma","After all, you always put those rare experiment samples together to fight each other, which is really brutal and wasteful."],["Morgana","Is it okay... I'm still curious how the headquarters could bear to let go of such talent like you..."],["Rosa","Wait, I have a new question..."],["","Once excluded from the conversation, Rosa directed her question to Paloma."],["Rosa","According to you, you've all undergone that arashi material renovation surgery? Could it be that Ada also..."],["Paloma","Of course, you can see it in my eyes..."],["Leopold","Allow me to explain."],["","Leopold interrupted Paloma's enthusiastic introduction. It was a question that required careful answering, but another silent participant also provided a timely report."],["Sloth","Vice Captain, that guy has arrived."],["","At some point, Sloth had already opened his eyes. No longer playing the role of a wallflower in the corner, he stood up with a tall stature similar to Leopold's."],["","If one didn't know his usual demeanor, at first glance he indeed presents a very reliable image."],["Leopold","I understand... Rosa, I'll explain to you later."],["Rosa","No, Ada, she actually..."],["Leopold","You did let her escape from those experiments, and that was the right choice, I assure you."],["","Leopold understood what Rosa was afraid of, which made his promise seem particularly reliable, allowing Rosa to relax."],["Rosa","Then why now...?"],["Leopold","Morgana, I need you to stay out of sight for a while. If the inspectors see you, it will be hard to explain."],["Morgana","Done already? Okay then, Rosa and I still have so much to talk about. Let her come with me for a short while for our routine report..."],["Leopold","No, Rosa will also follow us. No matter what, we won't let you be alone with her."],["Leopold","This is also one of the contract terms."]],"561003301":[["Paloma","Um..."],["Sapientia","Shh!"],["","Ignoring Sapientia's shushing, Paloma rolled her eyes and loudly grumbled while walking inside the base."],["Paloma","Why is she following us like this? Sapi's feeling nervous!"],["Sapientia","...Sigh? No, it wasn't me..."],["Veronica","..."],["","Ignoring Paloma's undisguised hostility and disgust, Veronica at the end of the team is carefully examining this old facility."],["","From the moment she disembarked from the ST and began moving through the hangar, she remained silent, scanning every corner. No one knew what she was contemplating and analyzing."],["Sloth","I feel the same way, I also want to ask this question."],["","Sloth yawned and glanced at Veronica behind him, continuing to walk listlessly."],["","He used to always be at the end of the team, but now it's his turn to be watched from behind, naturally making him feel uneasy."],["Leopold","Haha, trying to outsmart the Inspection Committee with paperwork, it really is..."],["Veronica","There is an additional clause for this mission. If the team is unable to carry out orders due to any unexpected circumstances, I will temporarily accompany the team as an external inspector until the cause of the incident is determined."],["Veronica","This is consistent with the additional clause from when Ada Diaz updated the management protocol back then—no direct interference with any of the squad's actions. Isn't that right?"],["Leopold","...That's right, but we're just following Ada's instructions. You should go to Captain Ada Diaz... Staying here watching us is just a waste of time."],["Veronica","A waste of time is good. When dealing with any unexpected events and reports, nothing is more reassuring than a waste of time... But so far, I've already discovered three issues."],["","Leopold sighed, completely giving up on opposing the unfeeling bureaucratic machine behind him."],["","Those who seem to follow the rules the most are often the ones who find loopholes to benefit themselves."],["Veronica","First, the Valkyrie had been classified as harmless due to a lifetime coma. How did she awaken?"],["Rosa","..."],["","This statement carries obvious hostility."],["","Rosa did not refute; anyone in the DL has ample reason to harbor hostility towards her, and those as flexible as the Reversion Squad are in the minority."],["Paloma","What does a lifetime coma mean? I didn't sign that diagnosis at the time..."],["Veronica","If she hadn't been unconscious, the Oceanic Conclave wouldn't have agreed to let the Reversion Squad handle the UNCS Valkyrie's containment."],["Veronica","Paloma, if you stick with that answer, withholding information will just be one more crime added to your charges later on..."],["Paloma","Hmm..."],["","Clearly, Paloma can't handle this kind of role either."],["","Adult problems need to be solved by adults."],["Leopold","No one could have predicted Rosa's awakening; it was unexpected for us as well, and I will explain it to you later."],["","Veronica smiled, pleased with Leopold's rebuttal under the rules; this is her area of expertise."],["Veronica","Secondly, establishing a containment site here violates the DL's intel security regulations."],["Leopold","That's because compliant garrison locations are influenced by the defense forces... Rosa Díaz's reputation in the DLAF... I think you should be well aware."],["Veronica","Oh? Is that really the only reason? Or do you think I don't know the \"story\" of these ruins?"],["Veronica","This was a research base established by Obsidian before the Border War, but it gradually became a deserted city due to the war reshuffling and distancing from major mining centers. In the eyes of veteran mercenaries, it was once an excellent hideout."],["Veronica","But at some point, bizarre urban legends began to circulate here. Beneath this city lie countless miners who died due to Obsidian experiments, and they have started to awaken, demanding all the regrets they had in life from the living."],["Veronica","The gangs stationed here began to be wiped out one after another, leaving no trace behind. Over time, this place became one that superstitious mercenaries kept their distance from."],["Veronica","And because of these rumors, this place instead..."],["Rosa","Won't be disturbed by unexpected guests, making it an excellent hiding spot."],["Veronica","..."],["","Rosa, without hesitation, took the deduction that should have been made by Veronica, as she was also observing and contemplating."],["","That's right, from this perspective, the answer becomes obvious... The so-called abandoned city and urban legends are merely means to drive away unexpected guests and interference."],["","The real purpose is to use these fabricated rumors to establish a naturally thriving no-man's land beneath this seemingly abandoned city... thus avoiding the watchful eyes of troublesome forces."],["","The true master of this area is still the Obsidian that created it, a private domain meticulously maintained by a woman named Morgana amidst the cracks of various forces."],["","Thinking of this, Rosa couldn't help but glance at Veronica. This newcomer DL inspector probably hasn't realized what kind of secret the Reversion Squad is hiding from her."],["Leopold","That's right, just as Rosa said."],["Leopold","As for the rumor you mentioned... Sorry, I haven't heard of it, but staying here for just a day or two should be fine, right?"],["Veronica","\"Just staying for a day or two\"... Oh, so it just happens that beneath this makeshift hideout, there's an arashi matter lab of remarkably high specification?"],["Veronica","Is this also something you \"just happened\" to discover while passing through?"],["Leopold","Hmm... Who knows... Paloma stumbled upon it while wandering around."],["Paloma","Yes, yes, I discovered it. After all, Sapi is so afraid of ghosts, the task of exploring this area had to be handed over to me!"],["Veronica","..."],["","A lie that is clearly stalling for time, yet cannot be directly exposed."],["Veronica","So, for this final question... how do you plan to evade it..."],["Veronica","Obvious evidence is sitting here in plain sight... Have you lost all regard for the Oceanic Conclave?"],["","Veronica stopped in her tracks and pointed to the deepest part of the hangar toward an ST, lurking in the shadows, yet still managing to exude a foreboding aura."],["Veronica","In the report on the containment of Rosa, it is stated that Ada Diaz should have only taken Rosa during that battle, and the Plutone piloted by Rosa should have fallen into the hands of either the UNCS or Obsidian."],["Veronica","Regardless of which report is examined, Plutone provides Rosa with a significant Boost capability. Some experts even point out that it was the main means by which Obsidian exercised control over Rosa during the late stages of the Blair Rebellion."],["Veronica","I'm curious how you managed to acquire this ST, which is considered a treasure by the UNCS, and why Rosa Díaz was given the opportunity to access it..."],["Veronica","Or did your captain conceal something in the mission report, not informing you of the details behind this?"],["Paloma","Correction, although it looks very similar... that's not the Plutone, it's the Erinys, modified once again."],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","If I told you that the ST was already here before we arrived in this city, would you believe me?"],["","This statement is not a lie, but this partial truth is no different from a lie when it comes from Leopold."],["Veronica","..."],["","Veronica frowned, carefully chewing over the roundabout statement."],["","A lie, undoubtedly a lie... However, anyone could see that Leopold could say it so calmly and demonstrate it..."],["","He had already prepared for the possibility that this information would not be passed up."],["Veronica","If I believe it, can I understand that you led Rosa into the trap prepared by Obsidian?"],["","She is indeed very talented, combining those fragmented clues from before, she has already started circling the edge of the truth."],["","But at the same time, judging from her somewhat cold expression, she probably realizes that her situation is no longer \"unfortunate\" but \"dangerous.\""],["Veronica","I must take immediate custody of Rosa Díaz—I'm taking her with me right now! If she gets into that ST, she'll tear through this place in minutes!"],["Rosa","I will not pilot the Erinys."],["","After a long silence, Rosa voiced her objection."],["Veronica","Do you think you have a say, Valkyrie?"],["","Veronica stared coldly at her, speaking of Rosa's past title that represented an executioner."],["Veronica","If you have any ideas, you can wait until the military tribunal or the Oceanic Conclave review to speak... For now, come with me. There are legal channels available for you to appeal your claims."],["Leopold","Rosa, leave this to me..."],["Rosa","No."],["Sapientia","Wait... wait a moment, the Vice Captain is doing this for you..."],["","Rosa sent away Sapientia, who was trying to provide her cover, and confronted Veronica."],["","She is not accustomed to standing behind others."],["Rosa","I know the DLAF and I have a deep-seated grudge, but now that Blair is dead and my girls have escaped those labs... I have no reason to be enemies with the DL."],["Rosa","I'm not trying to excuse the past; I will calmly accept the discipline from the DL, but..."],["","Rosa closed her eyes, and the blurred figure emerging in the darkness signified the long-awaited reunion."],["Rosa","I must meet Ada."],["","She opened her eyes and began her promises in the real world."],["Rosa","Whatever you want to know, please wait until Ada returns. You'll get all the answers in due course."],["Rosa","Until then, trust me, I will not take any actions harmful to the alliance or cause trouble for anyone."],["Rosa","As for that Erinys, I can feel its influence on me... so I will absolutely not pilot it."],["","Rosa bowed her head to Veronica, understanding the rules within the army. She didn't want her presence to cause trouble for Ada's teammate."],["","For this reason, she made her greatest effort and promised her first vow upon waking."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Why should I believe you?"],["Veronica","Or rather... what kind of person would unconditionally trust a killing machine that just woke up from a coma?"],["","A cruel yet justified response, leaving the person involved almost unable to refute."],["","She began her efforts, somewhat hurried and clumsy."],["Rosa","You can detain me now, or lock me up somewhere here. You can retrieve my ST... just wait for Ada to return, let her..."],["Veronica","Hmph..."],["Veronica","As arrogant as ever, Valkyrie..."],["Veronica","Is it because you always prevail on the battlefield that you simply assume everyone must follow your will?"],["Rosa","No, I never thought that..."],["Veronica","I'll say it again, I don't want to stop you from meeting your sister, but... keeping you here violates DLAF regulations, and your reunion with Ada shouldn't happen in a place filled with deception and traps."],["Veronica","To look at it another way... it's no longer just the Oceanic Conclave, but also [Madam] from the West Island, including those missing Obsidian, who are all focusing on the Reversion Squad because Ada took the Legacy."],["Veronica","If you want to see Ada, the best way is to come back with me. Go through the official channels and procedures, have this sister reunion done by the book. Get everything back in order."],["Veronica","If you consider yourself a competent sister, then please think more about your sister Ada Diaz and don't let her and her squad get into trouble again because of your recklessness."],["Rosa","I..."],["","The moment \"competent sister\" was spoken, Rosa's eyebrows suddenly furrowed."],["","Veronica knows what kind of words can hurt the person in front of her the most, and holding Rosa hostage—"],["","From her perspective, keeping Rosa, the most crucial card, in her hand—is her last means to escape this mire."],["","The Reversion Squad is using their privileges to engage in some unknown conspiracies, and they have become so confident that they completely disregard the inspectors of the Oceanic Conclave."],["","And the influence of that super pilot is indeed too high. Whether she stays to continue the investigation or immediately reports back, she is likely to face retribution from either Aida or the Reversion Squad."],["","If the Valkyrie from the UNCS in front of her chooses to compromise, she will have the trump card to balance both sides at the same time—at least for now, these sisters remain each other's weakness."],["Leopold","You're being a bit too aggressive, Veronica."],["","A hint of anger appeared on Leopold's face as he instructed his team members to block Rosa behind him, preparing for a new round of tug-of-war with this annoying agent."],["","Sapientia is somewhat at a loss, unsure if directly opposing the Inspection Committee is wise. Paloma, on the other hand, appears eager. And as for Sloth... he always manages to find a hidden corner."],["","But no one knows that the one to break this deadlock will be that person."],["Morgana","Could you please stop arguing? You two groups of guests, could you consider the host's opinion?"],["","A thin rope hangs down from the mechanic's platform, and a shadow slides down the rope, landing like a cat. The rope rebounds and retracts back into the launcher at her waist."],["Morgana","One, two, three... six. Good, everyone is here, saves me the trouble of finding people."],["Leopold","Didn't I tell you not to appear in front of the Inspection Committee members..."],["Morgana","I know, I know, but these are extraordinary times!"],["","Morgana's words remain flippant and casual, but from her somewhat hurried tone, it's clear that something seems to have happened."],["","Some things have already slipped beyond the control of this mastermind."],["Veronica","This uniform and emblem, indeed, are you guys...!?"],["Morgana","I am the manager of Obsidian's Predator forces under President Gideon, working with the Reversion Squad. This is the place I called them to."],["Morgana","Alright, enough introductions. Shut up for a while, okay?"],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","You are collaborating with the Predator forces in private, and must report immediately to the Oceanic Conclave... Damn, the signal here is blocked from the outside world!"],["","Faced with this explosive amount of information, Veronica's expression stiffens slightly, then she turns and strides towards her ST."],["","I... I must report immediately! The Reversion Squad, the strongest unit used to correct the alliance, has defected..."],["","But suddenly, a long blade slices past her side and lands in front of her, blocking her path."],["","The Obsidian woman smiled, maintaining her knife-throwing stance, and stared at her."],["Morgana","Leopold, can you help me hold her down and then explain properly?"],["Morgana","If we waste a few more minutes arguing with her, not only you, but my life will be in danger too."],["Leopold","...You better have a good reason afterward."],["","..."],["","After a struggle, everyone tied Veronica up and placed her on the ground. Now, except for the agent who could only make muffled sounds with a cloth stuffed in her mouth, everyone's attention was on Morgana."],["","What kind of news could shatter the previously maintained delicate balance and push everything towards an uncompromising direction."],["Morgana","During the recent regular communication, I received news that the headquarters' mobile guard unit is heading to this city, and their target is none other than the unique experimental subject—Rosa Diaz."],["Morgana","You probably know that our president has some conflicts with the group headquarters, and as subordinates, we are the same... For this Valkyrie of the NDF, we have been entangled for several rounds."],["Morgana","Even the former governor of the UNCS, Blair Bluecher, got involved... I don't need to tell you how critical the situation is, do I?"],["Leopold","You promised that this place would never be exposed."],["Morgana","Of course, do you know how much effort it took for me to run such a private place and avoid Eileen's spies?"],["Leopold","And how did the Obsidian troops from headquarters..."],["Morgana","Heh, well, that's something you should ask yourselves... Someone in the Reversion Squad has leaked intel to those corporate headquarters' lackeys... <yellow>There's a traitor among you!</yellow>"],["","Morgana interrupted Leopold, her gaze moving among the six. Compared to before, she now resembled a snake searching for its prey."],["","Anyone who met her gaze felt a bone-chilling cold seep in, causing them to instinctively look away, as if no secret could be hidden from her."],["Sapientia","Traitor... What does this mean..."],["Morgana","It's simple. Before you arrived here, someone leaked the meeting location, and the entire Milthus secret task force was mobilized... Even you can't stop them!"],["Sloth","Among us? That's impossible, that would be a huge problem..."],["Morgana","What's impossible? Of course, there's another possibility: one of you told someone else about the meeting point, and then that person leaked it to headquarters."],["Morgana","Is anyone willing to admit it? Anyone?"],["","No one answered, even Veronica, who had been constantly whining, stopped and just widened her eyes, looking around at everyone."],["Morgana","Looks like there aren't any fools here... So, there is indeed a mole."],["Leopold","Don't joke around, there's absolutely no one in my squad..."],["Paloma","That's not right, Vice Captain, there are more than just our squad members here, aren't there?"],["Rosa","..."],["Morgana","That kind of thinking is the most annoying... In my eyes, every one of you is equally suspicious."],["","..."],["","Morgana's judgment pierced the hearts of everyone like venomous fangs, and the poison named doubt began its encroachment, with silence as its initial symptom."],["Veronica","Mmmfff... Mfff-mfff..."],["Morgana","It seems the problem lady has something to say... Everyone is accepting it faster than I expected, so let her ask some more questions."],["","The cloth in Veronica's mouth is removed."],["Veronica","I have a general understanding of the situation... But how can you be sure someone really leaked the intel? Perhaps the HQ you mentioned has more sophisticated tracking methods than you."],["","She questioned the facts, but rather than trust, it seemed more like a logical confirmation."],["Morgana","That's impossible... It's not my arrogance, but if they really had such means, we would've been rounded up long ago. We wouldn't have had any room for maneuver."],["Morgana","Moreover, I have several locations like this at hand, yet they chose to launch a full-scale attack here, which must mean they have very accurate sources of information..."],["Veronica","There's another question: how did you determine the time of the leak? Why can you pinpoint it to <yellow>before arriving here</yellow>, rather than after..."],["Veronica","Even though this is a blind spot in the DLAF's coverage, it's still within their jurisdiction. How could a mobilization of that scale not alert the DLAF's suspicions?"],["","That's right, if the DLAF detects any anomalies, they will definitely alert the inspector who is on their way here, and also notify the Reversion Squad."],["Morgana","It's simple, because the leaker has a deep understanding of the DLAF's intel delay and operating rules. They found the perfect timing to exploit the gap between premature exposure and late failure... Therefore, the mole can only be someone among you."],["Morgana","Secondly, according to the intel from my informants, that person only leaked <yellow>this city</yellow>, not <yellow>this base</yellow> where we are currently located."],["","Before the Reversion Squad arrived in this city, they were unaware of the existence of this secret base. The leak could only have occurred after <yellow>the Reversion Squad received orders to rendezvous in the city</yellow> and <yellow>before arriving in the city</yellow>."],["Morgana","Or perhaps it's a decoy by the traitor, deliberately leaking only the city to mislead me... No, no, they probably didn't think that far. That would only narrow down the list of suspects..."],["Sloth","That would only clear Veronica of suspicion, as she hadn't been at the base long enough to gather the necessary intel for such a disguise... Quite a convenient way to brush off trouble..."],["Paloma","Right, what about those underlings she brought? Don't they also pose a risk of leaks?"],["Veronica","No, they didn't know the destination before coming with me. They coulnd't have leaked anything... But Rosa—what possible suspicion could there be against her?"],["Rosa","..."],["","With a purely rational judgment, she is exonerating herself from the object of her previous attack."],["","But the despondent one remained silent, neither agreeing nor disagreeing, as if none of this concerned her."],["Morgana","It's simple. Rosa's current abilities and state defy conventional understanding. We know no more about her than we do about what arashi material actually is."],["Morgana","Perhaps she unconsciously sent a message, or brainwashed someone to carry out the betrayal... No matter how far-fetched the possibility, it must be considered."],["Veronica","And also..."],["Morgana","You should gag her again."],["Veronica","Mmmfff... Mfff-mfff..."],["Sapientia","But if I keep thinking like this, wh-what do I do...?"],["Leopold","Alright."],["","Leopold halted the pointless suspicion, his words like a sharp blade cutting through all the chaos on the scene."],["Leopold","If your words are meant to make us suspect each other, they are completely meaningless. What we need to do now is not to find a traitor that may not even exist, but to think about what to do next."],["Morgana","Exactly! It's because of you that I dare to release these unsettling messages without reservation."],["","Morgana casts a look of admiration at Leopold, then walks forward, passing through the crowd, and picks up the long sword that previously blocked Veronica's path."],["Morgana","The silver lining is that the location of the base has not been exposed, allowing you to maneuver with the incoming advance team and weaken their search efforts in the city."],["Morgana","And I also have time to leave the city, find a way to contact the president, and bring reinforcements... Oh, the reason it took time is because of that thing your Captain Ada brought, making their meeting place impossible to trace..."],["Morgana","Of course, I'm not included in that."],["Leopold","In that case, we should also withdraw from this city together."],["Morgana","The moment you leave here, you'll be exposed to the detection range of various forces, and you'll be watched by their informants, fleeing with a burden... Is this really a good idea?"],["Leopold","Even so, getting the DL's shelter as quickly as possible is the best strategy..."],["Morgana","Is it really okay to let the <yellow>one who leaked the intel</yellow> go like this?"],["Leopold","..."],["","Morgana turned back, giving Leopold a meaningful look, and with a deft motion, she flipped the long sword in her hand and sheathed it behind her."],["Morgana","Regardless of your choice, the advance team will enter the city through the only entrance—the <yellow>suburban checkpoint</yellow>—in at most half a day. Try to get through this first."],["Morgana","And also... Rosa, just like in the past, if you want, you have a way to end all of this."],["Rosa","..."],["","She can bring everything to an end, but as in the past, it will bring irreversible consequences."],["Morgana","As for that traitor, if Rosa ultimately falls into the hands of HQ, I will find you. And before I kill you, I'll make you watch as I kill everyone you love."],["","As the launcher at her waist shoots out a rope, Morgana leaps into the shadows, gradually disappearing from everyone's sight."],["","As her presence completely fades away, she leaves behind one final warning."],["Morgana","I know, protecting others and such are the reasons that drive people like you to betrayal, but unfortunately, you have no choice."],["Morgana","So why not be an honest and trustworthy person in the end?"]],"561004101":[["","Have I been a good sister?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Certainly not."],["","Staring at the familiar ceiling, Rosa murmured to herself."],["","It was still the same operating room. After a brief discussion, Rosa was placed back here and would be released after dealing with the attack on the Obsidian headquarters."],["","The door was locked, both imprisoning her and protecting her."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","I can't go on like this. They're protecting me... I can't just lie here."],["","A familiar thought surged in, forcing Rosa to rise from the operating table and walk to the door."],["","But unfortunately, this time the door was locked."],["Rosa","Damn it!"],["","Agitated, Rosa tugged at the door a few times. She yelled out in frustration, hoping someone watching the surveillance would respond to her."],["","No response..."],["","She is certain that if no effort is made, the squad and that inspector will keep her detained until the incident is over... But since everything started because of her, is it really okay for her to just stay here?"],["","When they locked her up again, she should have resisted instead of reluctantly accepting this dead end."],["","This is also a sign of incompetence."],["Rosa","Is there really no way..."],["","As she thought about this, a phrase flashed through her mind."],["Morgana","Paloma, right? Are you interested in <yellow>returning</yellow> to work at Obsidian?"],["Morgana","Of course, I don't mean at headquarters. The president here can give you a much better deal... Even an immersive laboratory like this, built with masses of <yellow>arashi matter constructs</yellow>—it wouldn't be out of the question."],["","It was the information revealed by Morgana when she greeted Paloma, that many things in this research institute are mixed with <yellow>arashi matter</yellow>..."],["Rosa","...Open."],["","Holding her breath and concentrating, Rosa recalls the memories within her body, those memories of consciousness dwelling in darkness, memories of operating others' STs and opening fire on her companions."],["","The sensation of controlling external arashi matter had already been etched into her body. Back then she needed the amplification from her ST and backpack unit, but with the matter now flowing inside her..."],["Rosa","It opened... ugh..."],["","Like magic, the lock clicked open with a crisp sound. The path to the mystery has been unlocked."],["","But she immediately let out a painful groan, one hand supporting the door, the other hand on her forehead, panting."],["","This must be the side effect Paloma mentioned... Even a small action like unlocking a door gives her a piercing pain in her head."],["","Using her abilities in combat is now impossible."],["","After a brief respite, Rosa stepped out of the operating room, glanced around, and headed towards the ST storage as if escaping for the first time."],["","Soon, she had her first encounter with others in the ST storage."],["Sapientia","...Huh? How did she..."],["","While preparing the ST on the console, Sapientia noticed Rosa's figure. She first glanced around guiltily, then nervously lowered the platform to Rosa's side."],["Sapientia","Rosa, how did you get out of the operating room!"],["Sapientia","Didn't I tell you to stay put... Ugh... I need to quickly inform the others..."],["Rosa","Sapientia, listen to me first."],["","Rosa's sudden sternness froze the flustered Sapientia in her tracks—even though Sapientia was supposed to be the one in charge of the situation."],["Rosa","All of this started because of me. I want to do something, rather than just stay in the operating room waiting for the outcome..."],["Rosa","If it's you, you should understand... the feeling of wanting to do something for your companions."],["","Rosa still remembers when Sapientia stood between Paloma and Morgana, sternly rejecting that malicious invitation."],["","This girl may seem timid and insecure on the surface, but if it's for others, she might unleash abilities even she couldn't anticipate."],["","A complex expression appears on Sapientia's face. Being pointed out by Rosa like this, she instead reacts with a bit of shyness, avoiding Rosa's determined gaze."],["Sapientia","Well... alright... I also think it was wrong to lock you up like that—after all, you're fine now, Rosa, aren't you?"],["Rosa","Thank you for your trust, but I still need to convince the others..."],["Sapientia","Convince the others... Hmm... It would be nice if we could..."],["","The optimistic girl hesitated."],["Rosa","...What's the situation?"],["Sapientia","You might not have noticed, but ever since Morgana said those words, everyone's been acting strangely."],["Sapientia","Paloma has been paying more attention to us than ever, Sloth ignores any conversation outside of orders, and the Vice Captain locking you up like that doesn't sit right either... Most importantly, that inspector, she..."],["Rosa","How is she?"],["Sapientia","She said that because she and Rosa are definitely not traitors, <yellow>there must be a traitor within the squad</yellow> and then she left..."],["","Sapientia couldn't hide the panic on her face. It's hard for anyone to accept the possibility of a traitor among their companions, especially for a simple girl like her."],["Sapientia","I know everyone better than anyone else. I believe no one would choose to betray us... but given the current situation..."],["Rosa","It's not an exaggeration to say this is the worst-case scenario..."],["","This kind of suspicion is like a time bomb; every minute and second that follows is part of the countdown to its explosion."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Let's... let's not think about that for now... By the way, Rosa, how did you get out of that operating room? We clearly saw the Vice Captain close the door."],["","Seeing Rosa fall into gloomy thoughts because of her words, Sapientia felt a bit embarrassed and awkwardly changed the topic to lighten the mood."],["Rosa","..."],["","After a moment of thought, Rosa decided not to hide anything from the girl in front of her."],["","Without someone like her taking a stand and breaking free of this suspicion, the incident might never end."],["Rosa","As you expected, I can now sense and manipulate the arashi matter to a certain extent, and the door is equipped with mechanisms made of arashi matter..."],["Sapientia","...Huh? You can actually do that without any ST amplification?"],["Rosa","I know it's hard to believe, but..."],["","Rosa pondered how to describe that incredible feeling, but then she seemed to notice something and fell silent."],["Rosa","Sorry, but please help me keep this secret."],["Sapientia","Yes? What's going on..."],["","Following Rosa's gaze toward the entrance of the ST depot, a figure stepped in through the doors—it was Leopold."],["","He spots the two at once, clearly surprised to see Rosa here, and quickly rushes over while shouting not to move."],["Leopold","Rosa, aren't you supposed to be..."],["Rosa","Leopold? Then..."],["Sapientia","It was... it was me who opened the door for her to come here."],["","Rosa breathed a sigh of relief, seeing Leopold as one of the trustworthy choices, but Sapientia acted first."],["","She demonstrated her trust in Rosa through her actions."],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","But Sapientia, you shouldn't have the authority to open that door."],["Sapientia","Well... this... if it's just that level of encryption, I can easily crack it..."],["","\"I'm not good at lying,\" she had previously said—and she was not wrong. Her lies were full of holes compared to Paloma's, who lies as naturally as she breathes."],["","Leopold only had to press her slightly, and she immediately fell into a stammering state."],["Leopold","Forget it, the means don't matter... But I also said not to involve Rosa in the subsequent actions, as it would increase the risk of her being captured."],["","Unlike before, Leopold's tone was devoid of any jest, only commands."],["","The always weak Sapientia suddenly burst forth with courage that didn't belong to her."],["Sapientia","But... but isn't this strange!? Rosa's condition was clearly odd just now, and we locked her up without waiting for her to recover..."],["Sapientia","The test is already complete, and at this point, locking her up again only proves that we still don't trust her!"],["Leopold","This is a critical moment, and I must fulfill my duties as vice captain to ensure..."],["Sapientia","If you are the vice captain, you shouldn't have let the squad end up like this!"],["Sapientia","Rosa just told me she wants to do something for us, even someone outside the squad like her has noticed something's wrong, why are you..."],["Sapientia","Isn't it because of mutual trust that we've come this far?!"],["Leopold","..."],["Sapientia","I think that especially in times like this, we should show trust in each other..."],["Sapientia","Otherwise, wouldn't we be falling right into that traitor's trap, causing us to fall apart!?"],["","The situation has reversed, and now it's Sapientia pointing at Leopold."],["Leopold","...They've both said things like this to me."],["Sapientia","Huh?"],["Leopold","Don't worry, we're not at the point of mutual suspicion... It's just that those two want to handle this incident in their own way, which is why this misunderstanding occurred."],["Leopold","But you're right, even though we were sure of Rosa's recovery, we still excluded her in this way..."],["","Leopold stepped forward and apologized to Rosa."],["Leopold","I was so focused on bringing the situation under control that I didn't stop to think about how you felt... This is my failure as vice captain, so please don't report me to Ada later."],["Rosa","..."],["Leopold","I'm trusting you here, alright?"],["Rosa","I know..."],["","Rosa nodded, it was a good start."],["Sapientia","That's right, everyone should get along like this!"],["","Sapientia bounced around, celebrating the moment."],["Leopold","Heh, seeing you like this, I'm even more certain we can successfully complete this mission."],["Sapientia","Really... Rosa, if the Vice Captain guarantees it, then everything will be fine!"],["Sapientia","Although Ada is the captain in name, it's actually the Vice Captain who makes the detailed decisions. He always manages to judge whether the mission can proceed based on the existing conditions."],["Sapientia","Because of this, we've avoided several potential wipeouts led by Ada and Paloma."],["Rosa","Well... that's good news..."],["","In other words, if Leopold determines that the mission cannot be completed or the damage exceeds expectations, he will choose to abandon the mission."],["","Abandoning this mission means abandoning Rosa."],["Leopold","Alright, since it's confirmed we're allies... Rosa, it's time to reveal the secret I've kept from you."],["Rosa","About why I can sense you all..."],["Leopold","...Correct."],["","As he spoke, Leopold removed the neck guard from his combat suit."],["","Beneath his sturdy neck, a faint dark glow can be seen, emerging on the skin through the shadows of bones and blood vessels."],["Rosa","This... this is..."],["Leopold","The PAMS System, a Bionic Intelligence Frame developed by the DL, differs from the models mounted on ST. It is an improved arashi material implant."],["Rosa","...You're lying to me. How is this any different from the UNCS's Nova-Frame..."],["Sapientia","No, at least in terms of individual application, it's not as terrifying as you think, Rosa."],["","Sapientia rolled up her left sleeve, revealing a faint dark glow at the connection between the prosthetic and her body."],["Sapientia","Implanting this framework doesn't cause us any harm, and thanks to its processing support, my arm's movement's quite satisfactory..."],["","Sapientia gestured with her prosthetic, ending with a peace sign, verifying her words."],["Sapientia","Leopold's neck also bore old wounds from the great battle, which were fully healed only after the frame was implanted."],["Rosa","Really... no cost at all?"],["Sapientia","If used as a medical device, the computing power required is minimal, so there's indeed no cost..."],["","Sapientia remained silent. Judging by her reaction, she might have wanted to lie, but knowing her lies wouldn't fool Rosa, she found herself in a dilemma."],["Leopold","During combat, if the frame is linked with the ST, it will impose a corresponding load on the pilot based on the computational power invoked."],["Leopold","As long as the power is controlled properly, it won't cause any damage. I can guarantee that."],["Rosa","..."],["","No matter who it is, they can feel that these two are still hiding something."],["","Rosa closed her eyes, and what appeared before her was the tragic scene of the Epiphyllum girls being implanted with the Nova-Frame, a nightmare she couldn't shake off."],["Rosa","But on this island... there is no power without a cost. At least, I don't believe it."],["Leopold","That's right, this model is still a trial type, and very few pilots can match with it. As far as I know, it's only used within the Reversion Squad."],["Rosa","If it's Ada, she shouldn't accept something like this after leaving the NDF... Did you force her?"],["Leopold","This is also one of the means by which the DL controls us."],["","He finally said it."],["Leopold","Reversion Squad holds the highest executive authority of the DL on Milkhama Island, capable of independently confirming, investigating, and adjudicating any suspicious incidents within the DL. However, no power exists without oversight."],["Leopold","Once we make any moves harmful to the alliance, the <yellow>Oceanic Conclave</yellow> will pass a resolution to trigger the frame and execute us."],["Leopold","If there's any unauthorized dismantling of the frame, we'll be executed automatically."],["Rosa","So, Ada—?!"],["","Rosa suddenly stood up and grabbed Leopold's collar, even though compared to their physiques, it was like grabbing a piece of solid rock."],["","But she still held on very tightly."],["Rosa","Were you lying to me before? You said Ada wouldn't..."],["Leopold","I can only tell you that Ada's intelligence frame is different from ours. She's... <yellow>special</yellow>."],["Sapientia","Yes... it's true. According to our judgment, the execution initiated by the Oceanic Conclave will not affect Ada..."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Why is that?"],["Leopold","Even as allies, the information we can disclose to you is limited... Anything beyond this crosses the line."],["Leopold","You need to find Ada yourself to confirm more details."],["Rosa","I know..."],["Rosa","I'm sorry."],["","Rosa calmed down and released Leopold's collar, the latter offering no resistance, as he understood his sister's anger."],["Veronica","Haven't you crossed the line enough already?"],["","As the atmosphere slightly eased, another uninvited guest joined the conversation, with Veronica appearing in the trio's view at some point."],["","Unlike the previous Leopold, Rosa cannot sense her presence, proving she has not been tainted by any arashium implants and is a pure human."],["Veronica","And all this talk about working together... Even daydreams should have some limits, right?"],["Sapientia","It's not daydreaming; if anything, you're the one who..."],["Veronica","Me? I just don't want to be influenced by your blind optimism and fall into Obsidian's trap."],["Rosa","But if we keep doubting each other, we won't be able to handle Obsidian's attack at all."],["Rosa","You don't strike me as the type to simply oppose without offering anything constructive."],["Veronica","Of course, so I've been searching for your whereabouts since earlier... Here, put these on."],["","Veronica took out three electronic bracelets and distributed them to the three people. She was already wearing the same style on her wrist."],["Veronica","This is a monitoring device for the communication signal. If anyone's surroundings have an instrument transmitting a signal to an external channel, it will trigger an alarm to inform others of their location."],["Veronica","Although I wanted to input everyone's identity information and recording functions, time is really tight, and this is the limit of what can be done at the moment."],["Rosa","...Are you trying to prevent anyone from leaking information about the base again?"],["Veronica","If what that Predator girl said is true, then the location of this base is the bottom line you must defend."],["Sapientia","No... If you really trusted everyone, you wouldn't need something like this..."],["Veronica","I really don't understand your objection. Unless you're a traitor, you have nothing to worry about, do you?"],["Sapientia","But..."],["Leopold","Understood."],["","Before Sapientia could argue further, Leopold had already put on the bracelet."],["","After wearing it, the clasp automatically extended from the inside of the bracelet, securely fastening it to his wrist. It seems that removing it will require some special means."],["Veronica","By the way, the other two team members are cooperating well, now there's only..."],["Leopold","If you trust me, please also trust Agent Veronica."],["","Rosa didn't answer her, but silently put on the bracelet."],["","Sapientia looked around and reluctantly put it on."],["Veronica","That's better. I'll take off the bracelet after this incident is over."],["","Veronica nodded with satisfaction, then prepared to turn and leave, but was called from behind by Leopold."],["Leopold","Does that make you trust us?"],["Veronica","I never agreed to that."],["Veronica","In this situation of mutual suspicion, blind trust is a much greater danger than you might imagine. But..."],["","Veronica turned to look at Leopold, and the atmosphere she brought was much more relaxed than at the beginning."],["Veronica","Without a leader who can convince others, this situation would fall into a completely unsolvable quagmire."],["Leopold","From you, that's high praise—should I be flattered?"],["Veronica","This attitude is really annoying... Let me make it clear, I only follow your orders because you first agreed to my proposal."],["Veronica","At the same time, consider it a small token of appreciation for your help in repairing the ST..."],["","Her gaze quickly shifted to her ST in the hangar. The damage from the previous battle had been mostly repaired."],["Veronica","Were you the one responsible for the repairs?"],["Sapientia","No, although I'm the team's mechanic, it's been a bit overwhelming for me alone, so your ST was handled by the Vice Captain..."],["Leopold","If there's anything you're concerned about, feel free to check. I'll be here with Sapientia preparing the ST for the time being."],["Veronica","No need. With two people present, even if there is a traitor among you, it's hard to make any moves."],["","A judgment based on logic saves a lot of trouble double-checking."],["Rosa","So you can actually fix STs, too..."],["Leopold","Haha, is that enough to impress you? Managing this squad takes much more effort than you think."],["","According to Leopold, managing the Reversion Squad is no different from being a nanny."],["Veronica","You don't know what Leopold's been through...? Never mind, in any case, as a partner rather than an enemy, he is indeed someone trustworthy."],["","In other words, as an enemy, he's the type you'd least want to face."],["Rosa","What he's been through, huh..."],["Leopold","Alright, alright, if you keep praising me, I won't be able to keep a straight face."],["Veronica","But considering your past experiences, and given the current extraordinary times, I've given you so many opportunities... Once everything is over, not a single matter that needs settlement will be overlooked."],["Leopold","By then, Captain Ada should be back, and your issue should be discussed with her."],["","Leopold is indifferent to Veronica's threats."],["Veronica","Tch... But at the same time, I must emphasize one point..."],["Leopold","Every time you speak, it sounds like a nagging mom..."],["Veronica","I don't believe in the possibility of Rosa colluding with the enemy while unconscious, and I am clear about my own innocence, so there must be a traitor among your squad. Can you guarantee to root out that person?"],["Leopold","..."],["","With just one sentence, she brought everything back to freezing point."],["","This issue has always existed, it was just bypassed in a casual manner earlier."],["Veronica","Whether you can do it or not, I will do it for you..."],["Leopold","No need, and I don't believe there's a traitor among my team."],["Leopold","Even though I trust you, if I were to rank my trust, I would place them at the top..."],["Veronica","I know..."],["Leopold","But I can assure you of one thing..."],["","Leopold spoke while also looking at Rosa and Sapientia, addressing everyone present."],["Leopold","I will protect everyone."],["Leopold","No matter what, the traitor <yellow>cannot reveal</yellow> the location of this base."]],"561005101":[["","In the monitoring room, six people from the base sat together around the table, watching the screen wall."],["","Unlike the previous surveillance images of Rosa, it has now merged into a green pixel detection map."],["","A cluster of dense dots is approaching the city, as Morgana said, heading towards the city's only entrance—the <yellow>suburban checkpoint</yellow>."],["Sapientia","So... did I turn off the detector?"],["","After receiving Leopold's approval, Sapientia turned off the detector, and the entire screen plunged into darkness."],["Sapientia","This way, all electronic devices operating in the base were shut down..."],["Leopold","Good. Everyone, get your systems ready. We're launching an EMP to silence the city..."],["","The four members of the Reversion Squad rose, and apart from the light on Leopold's neck and Sapientia's shoulder, Paloma's prosthetic eye and Sloth's waist also glowed."],["","Rosa could feel the abundant and calm arashi particles in the base gradually becoming disordered and trembling, like a school of fish in the ocean whose order was beginning to collapse..."],["","In an instant, the school of fish exploded, countless arashi particles burst out, causing Rosa to instinctively cover her face."],["","But her body didn't feel anything, and this dissonance between spirit and flesh left her somewhat dazed."],["","The pulse also ended at that moment."],["Paloma","Ah... As expected, these components snatched from Lukmund are useless. These imitations are all scrapped after just one use..."],["","Paloma staggered out of the room, looking at the pulse weapon emitting blue smoke, and muttered."],["","Not just her, the other three operators are not in good condition either, even Leopold Ashford quietly used his hand to support himself on the table to maintain balance."],["","Although it is a four-person link, even if it is a replica, the cost of activating this weapon is enormous for them, as it should have been wielded by the \"Legacy.\""],["","A weapon driven by the pinnacle of the PAMS System, Newman's brain."],["Leopold","With this, the city and its surroundings lose all functioning electronics, meaning the traitor's communication setups can't link to Obsidian, and their autonomous puppets will be completely paralyzed."],["Sapientia","During this period, our electronic devices also enter a state of silence, and the monitoring and detection equipment within the base cannot operate."],["Veronica","No need to worry—we still have her..."],["Rosa","According to the plan, I will stay in the operating room to monitor the base periphery."],["","Right now, aside from Rosa's ability to control a small number of autonomous units, the most critical assistance she can provide is intel collection."],["","STs or any enemies using arashi technology approaching the base cannot escape her perception range, which is akin to cheating in intel warfare."],["","When the enemy's main target is her, this is the way to maximize her abilities."],["Leopold","Please."],["","Leopold nodded to Rosa, then issued the next instructions."],["Leopold","According to the previously scouted forces, Sapientia, Paloma, and Sloth, the three of you will strike to meet the enemy. The goal is to exterminate the enemy near the checkpoint."],["Leopold","Veronica and I will remain stationed at the base, utilizing Rosa's sensing abilities to ensure no enemies reach the base periphery."],["Sapientia","Understood!"],["Paloma","The Vice Captain isn't going... I feel like I can't slack off..."],["Sloth","..."],["Paloma","Sloth thinks so too, right? This time just..."],["Sapientia","Pa-lo-ma!"],["Paloma","Alright, alright, I understand..."],["","Sapientia pulled Paloma out of the meeting room, but Sloth still didn't move. It wasn't just because of the toll on his body; he seemed to be pondering something."],["Sloth","Vice Captain, do I really have to go on this mission?"],["Sloth","It's not that I'm afraid of trouble or anything—well, maybe that's seventy percent of it—but I just feel..."],["","During the conversation, his gaze shifted to Veronica, which made his meaning quite clear."],["Veronica","I know some of you still don't trust me, so if you send me out, it would only make people more worried, wouldn't it?"],["Sloth","..."],["Leopold","This is an order."],["Sloth","...Sigh."],["Sloth","Understood."],["","Dropping his objections, Sloth also left the monitoring room."],["Rosa","Then I'll go to the operating room and stand by."],["","Rosa also got up, left the monitoring room, and closed the door."],["","Back in the operating room, it had somehow become a place that felt like her own room, creating a sense of familiarity."],["","Rosa sat on the operating table, waiting was more mentally exhausting than she had anticipated. It felt like a lot of time had passed, but she could still sense everyone in the base, proving that the three hadn't set out yet."],["Rosa","..."],["","Though it seemed a bit boring on the surface, she was already accustomed to such waiting."],["","She wanted to focus her consciousness on perceiving the arashi matter, but like focusing on one's breathing only to find it harder to breathe, it had the opposite effect."],["","This ability, akin to an instinct, is best used when left to its natural course."],["Rosa","...Who is it?"],["","Suddenly, she felt someone approaching her door."],["Rosa","Is there something wrong?"],["","Rosa got up and walked towards the door, but in that brief moment, the figure outside had already gone."],["Rosa","..."],["","A bit of doubt arose in her heart, but Rosa sat back down. Maybe it was just the team members doing a final sweep of the base."],["","Before long, the communicator transmitted the voices of others talking."],["Sapientia","Well... let's set off..."],["Paloma","Go, go!"],["Sloth","...Sigh."],["","Even in the operating room where Rosa is located, the sound of STs starting up can be heard, and then the entire base falls into silence again."],["","The first battle against Obsidian has begun."],["","Approximately ten minutes have passed—Rosa's estimate, as there is no clock in the room."],["","Even if there was one, it would've been destroyed in the previous pulse attack."],["","Rosa increasingly feels that waiting is not suitable for her. In the past, no matter the time or situation, she had always charged ahead, carrying everything on her own."],["","This kind of teamwork, this reliance on others—it's something she still cannot get used to."],["Rosa","But... Ada, you do have a great group of partners."],["","That's right. Her own disposition doesn't really matter—knowing that Ada has a group of partners around her who can rely on and trust each other makes her feel an unusual sense of relief."],["","What she gave up back then was not entirely meaningless..."],["Sapientia","V-Vice Captain! They both ran off somewhere, and the defense line has been breached..."],["","..."],["","As she was thinking this, Sapientia's panicked voice came through the communicator, even sounding tearful."],["Leopold","Paloma, Sloth, report the current situation."],["","Leopold quickly responded, his voice remaining calm."],["Paloma","Huh? Sapi, you're really making a fuss over nothing. I'm just nearby, aren't I?"],["Sloth","Rest assured, the enemy will not approach the base periphery."],["Leopold","Enough, you two move towards the checkpoint immediately to support Sapientia..."],["","Rosa has also gradually gotten used to the team's atmosphere. Maybe the process is always chaotic, but in the end, everything is still within their plan."],["","Leopold sent these three people, surely having anticipated the current situation, so..."],["Rosa","..."],["","Listening to the noisy communication channel, the idle Rosa suddenly sat up abruptly from the operating table."],["Rosa","Everyone! We've detected a Predator-type signal very close to the base!"],["Sloth","How is that possible? No..."],["Veronica","Rosa, can you pinpoint the exact location of the enemy?"],["Rosa","Sorry, I can only sense that they are very close to the base, but beyond that..."],["Leopold","Veronica, there should only be two entrances to the base, and the enemy is most likely on the west side near the checkpoint..."],["Veronica","Understood, I'll handle the guy outside. You stay on alert for other emergencies inside the base; this could be one of the enemy's traps."],["Leopold","Alright, it's up to you."],["Leopold","The rest of you, continue with your tasks. Leave the base periphery to us. Don't let your support movements expose the base's location."],["Paloma","Got it~"],["Sloth","...Understood."],["Sapientia","Hurry... hurry over here, Paloma!"],["Rosa","..."],["","As Sapientia's final call echoes, the communicator falls silent once more. If it weren't for the need for a message requiring full synchronization, everyone would have their own dedicated combat channel for communication."],["","Rosa opened her mouth, wanting to say something or offer some help, but the intel she had was indeed limited."],["","There are enemy signals around the base, and that's all."],["","Even if she wants to offer some advice, it probably won't be better than the judgment given by Veronica or Leopold. It's better to just wait patiently."],["","And shortly after Veronica moved out, the signal disappeared—indicating that the enemy had been successfully annihilated."],["","Silence and waiting are the better choice at the moment."],["Rosa","No, there must be something I can do."],["","Rosa stood up and walked towards the door, placing her hand on the doorknob."],["","She hadn't mentioned to Leopold that she could open doors using arashi matter yet. Showing him now could very well broaden the range of tactical options available..."],["Rosa","...Huh?"],["","Everything is operating just like last time, but there's a noticeable obstruction. It's not a control difficult, it's.."],["","The lock is jammed."],["","A structure that should have operated smoothly is immobilized due to the intrusion of a foreign object."],["","The incredible superpower that everyone talks about was easily broken just because of a foreign object that is not arashi material."],["Rosa","Could it be at that time... No, the urgent task now should be to report to Leopold..."],["","The temporary anomaly did not completely unsettle Rosa. She can sense that Leopold is still within the base, and if she reports now, everything might still be within control."],["","Maybe it's just a prank by Paloma, or perhaps the door lock has naturally deteriorated due to lack of maintenance, or maybe..."],["","Regardless, a slight unease has begun to grow in her heart. Just a few more unusual occurrences, no matter how small, and this unease will turn into tension, even fear."],["","What Rosa didn't expect was that the next unusual occurrence would come so quickly, officially marking the event's entry into the next stage..."],["Rosa","What... What's going on, what happened?"],["","The bracelet on her wrist suddenly vibrated, causing Rosa to pause her report, and then a glaring red coordinate appeared on it."],["Leopold","Damn... Veronica, does this mean..."],["Veronica","Activated? But this coordinate... how is it possible...?"],["Leopold","All personnel, proceed to the coordinates on your wrist display, and those near the coordinates, cease movement immediately!"],["Leopold","Someone has sent out coordinate information, we must immediately determine the details..."],["","..."],["","The base's coordinates have been leaked."],["Rosa","No... How could it be... Someone leaked it..."],["","The small, accumulating unease continued to swell within Rosa, filling her entire body and leaving her mind blank."],["","Afterwards, the only thought left in her mind was that she must do something."],["Rosa","Leopold, hurry and open the door to the operating room!"],["Leopold","Rosa? Stay in the operating room. I'll keep the base safe."],["Rosa","No, I must..."],["","Leopold refused Rosa's request, a decision made out of rational judgment."],["","But Rosa didn't see it that way."],["","Just like during the riot, now she must step forward to ensure everyone's safe retreat."],["","At this moment, she needs to stand up to prevent her partners from falling into danger."],["","Besides that, she doesn't know what else she can do."],["","So, her hand reached for the door handle again."],["Rosa","Open... for me..."],["","The more she used her abilities, the more it felt like driving a sharp spike into her own skull, and the door lock emitted a corresponding wail."],["","But at this moment, Rosa could no longer feel her pain or limits. She must..."],["","Must..."],["","Her will had brought no miracle."],["","All she waited for was darkness."]],"561005301":[["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["Rosa","Hmm... Mmmfff..."],["","Slowly opening her eyes, her sluggish brain gradually started to function, and Rosa realized she had fainted on the ground."],["Rosa","Where the... Oh right..."],["","After discovering someone leaked the base coordinates, I was eager to leave the operating room and overused my abilities, which led to my coma."],["","As Paloma said, in the real world, there aren't many things that can be overcome by will alone."],["Rosa","What's the situation now? I need to quickly tell everyone what happened..."],["","Rosa, somewhat flustered, grabbed the communicator beside her, preparing to contact others, when the door was suddenly pulled open."],["Sapientia","Oh, you're here... But why are you sitting on the floor?"],["Rosa","Sapientia, the battle outside has already..."],["Sapientia","The battle ended a while ago, and now everyone is in the monitoring room preparing for a meeting."],["Sapientia","I called you several times on the communicator, but you didn't answer. Everyone was a bit worried, so they sent me to check on you."],["Rosa","Sorry, something happened just now, so I didn't notice... Did you discover anything new?"],["Sapientia","There are some things... Follow me first, and I'll tell you the general situation on the way."],["","It's better to listen to what exactly happened first before deciding whether to disclose the situation here, especially since she promised not to misuse her abilities before..."],["","Moreover, if there really was a leak incident, it would have happened outside the base, and what happens inside the base interior shouldn't be too relevant."],["","So Rosa thought."],["Paloma","Whoa! Finally showed up, eh?"],["","As they entered the meeting room, Paloma greeted them, waving excitedly."],["Sloth","Seems like your habit of being late is worse than mine..."],["Rosa","Sorry, did I delay the meeting?"],["Paloma","No big deal. The Vice Captain's the real king of being late this time. He used to always be the first one to arrive..."],["Sapientia","He should be here soon, right? Didn't he just say he was checking in the hangar to see if anyone's ST had a tracking device placed on it?"],["Paloma","What's the point of checking that now? The base's coordinates have already been leaked anyway..."],["Rosa","The base's coordinates... have really been leaked?"],["","Even though Sapientia explained the situation on the way, it's still hard to believe such a fact."],["Paloma","It seems you really weren't listening to what we were talking about on the channel just now..."],["","Paloma speaks, pointing to the corner where Veronica leans in the shadows."],["Paloma","She's the traitor. In a moment, we'll capture her just like before. Rosa, remember to lend a hand."],["Veronica","..."],["","Unlike in the past when she would counter every provocation against her, Veronica simply keeps a stern face, looking to the side."],["","The situation in the monitoring room is now quite clear. The team members sit in unison on one side, forming a standoff with Veronica."],["","Since Sapientia brought her along, Rosa also took a seat with the squad."],["","Now, we just need Leopold to come and give the final verdict to determine Veronica's future situation."],["","Looking on the bright side, no matter how bad it gets, it won't be worse than the situation with Morgana."],["Leopold","Sorry to keep you waiting."],["","As everyone fell into silence, making the atmosphere somewhat oppressive, Leopold pushed the door open and entered."],["","Upon seeing the confrontational seating in the conference room, he unexpectedly sat on Veronica's side."],["Leopold","I just checked the communicators of each ST and found no traces of information being sent to the outside world, perhaps..."],["Paloma","Covering comms traces on that level? Even someone like Sapi could knock it out in ten minutes."],["Sapientia","Why use me as an example...? Although it is indeed quite simple..."],["Leopold","That's right, this cannot serve as proof of innocence... At a mimum, it cannot be used to deny the coordinates were leaked that way."],["Leopold","Is there anyone who still doesn't understand the severity of the coordinate leak...?"],["Sapientia","Could it be... could it be that it's already..."],["","Abort the mission... even though Sapientia didn't say it, everyone thought of it."],["Leopold","It's already infinitely close. I can't risk everyone's lives on an impossible objective, but... before that, I still need to collect more clues as a basis for judgment."],["Leopold","So, Veronica, now is your time to prove your innocence."],["Veronica","..."],["","Veronica steps out from the shadows and takes a seat at the table, officially joining the conversation."],["Veronica","Let's go over the process of how the leak occurred, shall we?"],["Leopold","No problem, there might be people on site who are not fully aware of the situation."],["Rosa","..."],["","Sapientia had also joined the battlefield midway, so the content she had synchronized with Rosa was quite limited."],["Veronica","The turning point of the entire interception battle likely began with the <yellow>negligence</yellow> of Paloma and Sloth, which ultimately allowed Sapientia's defensive line to be breached."],["Paloma","Although you're speaking ill of me again, it's indeed true."],["Sloth","Ultimately, no enemy reached the vicinity of the base, so it's not considered negligence, right?"],["Leopold","Afterward, I issued adjustment instructions to them, and at that time, you still hadn't <yellow>piloted the ST away from the base</yellow>, until..."],["Rosa","I sensed the <yellow>sudden appearance</yellow> of enemies around the base periphery and sounded the alarm. Then Veronica ordered the attack, right?"],["Veronica","That's correct. Following Leopold's instructions, I discovered a wandering enemy at the entrance of the Central Square on the west side of the base and destroyed them..."],["Sloth","That enemy..."],["Veronica","Do you have anything to confirm? The <yellow>wreckage</yellow> of the destroyed enemy still exists, you can go investigate."],["Sloth","No, it's nothing."],["Veronica","Of course, Rosa should also confirm this. The reaction you sensed should have disappeared, right?"],["Rosa","Indeed."],["","Until now, these are universally acknowledged facts."],["Veronica","Then I contacted Sloth to confirm the direction in which the main force of the enemy fled after making headway, and proceeded to the Southern City to clear them out."],["Veronica","Those guys were tougher than I imagined, and I ended up surrounded by them. Then, during the stalemate, the leak alarm was triggered..."],["Paloma","The alarm... is it this anti-leak bracelet? As long as it senses any device sending messages to targets other than us, it starts beeping incessantly and synchronizes the coordinates to other bracelets..."],["Paloma","Hehe, it feels like discovering a murder scene and broadcasting it to the entire room."],["Leopold","The location indicated by the anti-leak alarm was in the Southern City, and when Paloma and Slo arrived, they only found you there."],["Veronica","...Correct."],["Paloma","So, you don't have much room to argue, right? At that time, the Southern City showed you were the only one present..."],["Veronica","I was indeed in the Southern City during the leak, but..."],["Veronica","Can you two provide evidence that you weren't at the scene?"],["","Without evidence to prove your innocence, you drag others into suspicion."],["","This is the direction Leopold pointed out to Veronica on the battlefield."],["Paloma","At... at that time, I was in the suburbs. As for evidence, well, it's not like I don't have any, but now..."],["Veronica","Sloth, what's your status over there?"],["","Ignoring Paloma's evasive remarks, Veronica turned her attention to Sloth."],["Sloth","I'm at the Central Square. As for evidence... why don't you first tell me what exactly you're trying to prove?"],["Veronica","It's simple: unless you can account for my exact whereabouts during the time I was surrounded, you can't rule out the possibility that I leaked the information."],["Veronica","You could have sent the intel from the Southern City first, then left ahead of time, and afterward doubled back to the scene pretending it was your first arrival, shifting all suspicion onto me."],["Veronica","I know my own innocence, so I conclude that the traitor is among you."],["Veronica","And if you give me some more time, I promise I can find the evidence..."],["Leopold","Veronica..."],["","Leopold reached out to hold back the increasingly aggressive Veronica, who was about to slam the table. She could only express her determination with a fierce glare."],["Leopold","What she said is not wrong. That method is possible. We cannot label Veronica as a traitor without proof."],["Sloth","This is an absolute mess..."],["Sapientia","So... so what the Vice Captain means is, you trust her more than everyone else..."],["Veronica","That's why I hate this kind of thinking... Instead of doubting your companions, just blaming everything on outsiders to make everything go smoothly..."],["Veronica","Isn't this the behavior of a traitor?"],["Sapientia","I... How could I be..."],["","As Veronica shifted accusations onto her, Sapientia immediately panicked. Luckily, she had that pink-haired one to back her up."],["Paloma","Hey, that's impossible, right?"],["Veronica","But at the time of the incident, no one could confirm her whereabouts, right? Maybe the chaos caused by the checkpoint being breached was part of her plan..."],["Paloma","What you said earlier does make some sense, but suspecting Sapi is ridiculous."],["Paloma","After all, if Sapi were to send information from the checkpoint to the Southern City, she would've had to pass through the area where Sloth and I were located, not to mention making round trips to cover her tracks."],["","This is a fact. From the city's map, it can be understood that the west of the Southern City is the suburbs, and the northwest is the central city."],["","Not to mention whether it's possible to complete the round trip in such a short time, the journey from the checkpoint to the Southern City must pass through the area where the other two are located."],["","Such an unusual move will definitely be noticed by others."],["Veronica","Is that so... It seems she's simply turning a blind eye to the facts."],["Sapientia","Well... maybe you're right... but I still don't want to doubt my companions!"],["Sloth","I think so too, it's really too troublesome."],["Rosa","Must we doubt our companions..."],["Paloma","But what the girl said isn't wrong. If we bully her like this, we become the unreasonable ones."],["Veronica","Teaming up on someone like this... come on, if you let it go on, it'll just keep escalating. Isn't it time for you to step forward and put things right?"],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","I think..."],["Rosa","Sorry, may I say a few words?"],["","While everyone focused their attention on Leopold, Rosa, who always seemed like an outsider, suddenly seized the opportunity to speak."],["","Indeed, precisely because she wasn't caught in the whirlpool of arguments and wasn't on either side of suspicion, she might be able to offer a more impartial opinion."],["","Leopold nodded, expressing his approval of her actions."],["","At this moment, Rosa recalled the powerless moments in the operating room earlier."],["","Perhaps now is the time she has been waiting for, the time to do something."],["","I <yellow>must</yellow> seize this opportunity."],["Rosa","Instead of looking for suspects, why don't we first think about which individuals are trustworthy?"],["Sapientia","Trustworthy... Isn't everyone..."],["Rosa","No, Sapientia, emotional trust alone cannot convince others; more concrete evidence is needed..."],["Veronica","I see... Apart from Sapientia, who was just proven, you and Leopold can also prove that you have both been at the base all along, right?"],["Rosa","That's right, I can always sense Leopold's implant signal. He definitely hasn't left the base."],["Leopold","I can confirm that Rosa's ST shows no signs of activation. She has been in the operating room all along."],["Veronica","Alright, does anyone want to challenge the evidence of these three?"],["Veronica","This will determine whether the traitor will take control."],["","No objections."],["Veronica","There's no doubt, from the current situation, Sapientia, Leopold, and Rosa are not suspected of being traitors."],["Veronica","You continue."],["Rosa","Thank you... So I think, if an investigation or discussion is needed, it would be a better decision to leave it to the three of us at this stage."],["Sapientia","What... Rosa, are you also suspicious of everyone?"],["Rosa","Sapientia... Sorry, I have to do this now."],["","I wonder if this slightly cold apology can heal the wounds of this girl."],["Rosa","If there really is a traitor, they might interfere with the direction of the investigation and discussion, or lie based on others' testimonies to cover up the truth."],["Paloma","Wow, that sounds like something I would do."],["Sloth","But is there really enough time to conduct an investigation? The coordinates have already been leaked..."],["Rosa","No, from the current information, there is no clear evidence to prove that someone among us has sent the <yellow>base coordinates to Obsidian</yellow>..."],["Paloma","But it has been confirmed that someone has sent <yellow>coordinate-related information</yellow> to Obsidian."],["Rosa","But couldn't it be that someone outside of us did it? Maybe there are other possibilities behind this..."],["Leopold","If there's such a possibility, are you confident you can find it now?"],["Rosa","I... can."],["","This is a promise that must be made."],["","Just like in the past, if she hesitates now, everything will fall apart."],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","Very well, I agree with Rosa's perspective."],["Leopold","As for the concerns Sloth has... it's just the advance team coming over now, so there should be several hours available for investigation."],["Leopold","Whatever actions we take next, if we can't identify the traitor beforehand, everything will be in vain."],["Leopold","I can't predict whether the plan will work under such variables."],["Paloma","I have no objections either!"],["Sloth","As long as I'm not the one doing it..."],["Veronica","Judging from the current situation... Hmph, can I only trust you?"],["Sapientia","..."],["Rosa","Sapientia..."],["Sapientia","Rosa, can you promise me you'll clear my partners of suspicion?"],["","A single inquiry made Rosa feel an undeniable sense of alienation."],["","She said <yellow>my</yellow>, not <yellow>our</yellow>."],["","At this moment, Rosa has already betrayed the trust she once gave and is now in the opposing camp."],["","But Rosa has long been accustomed to this feeling of being misunderstood by others... It's something she must get used to."],["","Unable to be of use in battle, she can at least break this deadlock by bearing the accusation of doubting others..."],["","As long as, in the end, it brings a good outcome for everyone, that's enough."],["","So... for now, she cannot make this promise."],["Rosa","Sapientia, sorry..."],["Rosa","All I can do is find out the truth."]],"561006101":[["","After discussion, the subsequent action plan was confirmed."],["","Now that the base coordinates have been exposed, the original operational plan surrounding the base is terminated. Next, we will engage in guerrilla warfare throughout the city with the Obsidian forces arriving one after another."],["","This combat strategy can both disperse the Obsidian forces, making it difficult for them to determine Rosa's exact location, and meet the need for investigations in various areas."],["","As for what needs to be done for the investigation, it is to confirm the exact location of each person at the time of the leak."],["","Therefore, everyone will return to the area they were in at that time, wait for the investigators to arrive, and provide evidence to prove their innocence."],["","As for the members of the investigation team... of the original three, due to Sapientia's voluntary withdrawal, only Rosa and Leopold remain."],["Sapientia","I'm sorry, but even now, I can't agree with your choice, so at least... please allow me to withdraw from this investigation."],["Veronica","Turning three into two? That's even better, as too many people gathering together can easily attract Obsidian's attention."],["Veronica","Also, acting alongside two members of the Reversion Squad could cloud Rosa's judgment... Two can keep each other in check, preventing a traitor from manipulating the whole situation..."],["Sapientia","..."],["","Ultimately, Sapientia chose to stay at the base."],["","This is not a meaningless choice. There are still many defense facilities within the base that can be utilized, causing considerable small trouble for the Obsidian troops coming to investigate."],["","If some developments do not go smoothly and effective maneuvering in the city is not possible, everyone will still need to return here and prepare for a decisive battle with the enemy's main forces."],["","Finally, regarding some matters related to the investigation, everyone has made an agreement that they must not <yellow>lie</yellow> during the subsequent evidence collection."],["","Regardless of the purpose, once a lie is exposed, the person will immediately be deemed a traitor."],["","Unlike Sapientia, who has no talent for lying, the three suspects need this constraint to prevent the investigation from going astray."],["Paloma","Okay, okay, I understand..."],["","You could say the greatest uncertainty now had an extra layer of insurance, allowing everyone to secretly breathe a sigh of relief."],["","Before the investigation officially began, there was a small interlude."],["","It happened during a conversation before the two investigators headed to the hangar."],["Rosa","...Leopold, there's something I want to ask you."],["Leopold","Let's hear it, Detective. As an assistant, I will definitely answer any questions."],["Rosa","This is not the time for jokes... My question is, why were you able to make such unrealistic promises before the action started?"],["Leopold","No matter what, the traitor <yellow>cannot reveal</yellow> the location of this base."],["Leopold","What I said back then... You really know how to expose someone's shortcomings. Can't you just take it as an old man's empty words?"],["Rosa","Some leaders use lies to encourage their subordinates at critical moments, but I can feel that you only said those words with absolute confidence."],["Rosa","Even now you're still completely at ease, not the least bit nervous about the traitor's leak."],["Leopold","Is it that feeling again... If it were anyone else, I might tell them not to trust such elusive things, but with you, it's particularly convincing..."],["Rosa","So, what exactly was your basis for making such a judgment?"],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","It's simple—I trust my team."],["","Clearly, it's another baseless testimony, yet from Leopold's mouth, it seems particularly powerful, like an irrefutable fact."],["Leopold","Didn't Veronica say at the time that the traitor was among the squad? And since I believed they would never betray us, I naturally assumed no leak would occur."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Then why are you participating in this investigation now?"],["","Rosa's implication is quite simple: if Leopold truly trusts his teammates, then he should choose to withdraw like Sapientia."],["Leopold","That's just one choice... Rosa, if something similar happened among those <yellow>partners you truly trust</yellow> outside, what would you do?"],["Rosa","They won't do that."],["Leopold","Didn't I say <yellow>if</yellow>? You shouldn't avoid this possibility..."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","I would eliminate this possibility before it happens."],["Leopold","Haha, that's a Valkyrie-style answer... Are you preparing to take on all of that by yourself?"],["Leopold","Just as you're doing now."],["Rosa","Because they're very important to me, so..."],["Leopold","That's why it's even more important to uncover the truth, rather than avoid that possibility."],["Rosa","...What?"],["Leopold","When it comes to things like determination, everyone is more or less the same. What matters is the decision-making made under that determination."],["Leopold","Both Sapientia and you chose to escape, which is also a form of realization, but I think there's no need for it at all... Since you trust your partners, you should do everything possible to prove their innocence."],["Leopold","Even now, I still believe the traitor is not among us."],["Rosa","..."],["","Regardless of ability, this might be the reason why Leopold can earn everyone's trust."],["Leopold","Of course, if the official captain were present, she might have taken the same approach as you."],["Leopold","This is the choice that only she and the past you could have."],["","Those who exceed any limits of reason can escape all this without punishment."],["","The ones Leopold refers to as Rosa and Ada are such reckless individuals."],["Rosa","...I understand, but there's one more thing I need to tell you."],["","With no room left for rebuttal, Rosa recalled that piece of intel—it felt almost like a piece of petty retaliation."],["Rosa","I can operate the surgery room's door lock through my mind to open the door."],["Leopold","...Oh? That's quite surprising. I knew Sapientia wouldn't open the door for you, but I didn't expect this situation."],["Rosa","That's not the point... Before everyone went out to intercept the Obsidian troops, I sensed that a squad member had come to the door of the operating room and tampered with it."],["Rosa","Maybe something was placed inside the door lock, preventing me from leaving the operating room when the alarm went off..."],["Leopold","Are you suggesting that the squad member is a traitor?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","No, it's just a possibility..."],["","This is indeed not conclusive evidence."],["","In the case where Sapientia is not a traitor, she doesn't understand how that person obtained intel about the door lock, nor why they would lock her in the operating room."],["","After all, if she's a traitor colluding with the enemy, Rosa should leave the base, making it easier for Obsidian to target her..."],["","If their goal is the truth, this will also be a puzzle that must be solved."],["Leopold","Hahaha... Since you're willing to tell me this, can I take it as you truly starting to trust me?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","No... I didn't before..."],["Leopold","That's a good thing, after all, we're partners from now on. An assistant who isn't trusted by the detective is of no use, right?"],["","While they were conversing, they had already arrived at the hangar, standing before the STs they were about to board."],["Rosa","...Understood."],["Rosa","If that's your mindset, then after this, I won't hold back anymore."],["","With that, Rosa strides towards the ST prepared for her."],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","Finally, I can talk like a regular person."]],"561007301":[["","Enemies are not human."],["","Paloma strives to explain this discovery to Rosa and Leopold Ashford. After feeling like she's just talking to a brick wall, she decides to let the evidence speak for itself."],["Paloma","Not far from here, there's a temporary research lab I set up using base equipment. There should still be some... Oh, right, maybe they can help prove my alibi."],["Rosa","Them..."],["","Not human, that's how Paloma described the enemies."],["Paloma","I've done quite a bit of homework recently while working with the Predators. If this technology is properly utilized, it has great potential. But after looking at the headquarters' most recent results, none of it makes much sense."],["Paloma","Once you've seen it, you'll understand. Rebirth technology? It's basically debirth technology!"],["Paloma","But it's really strange... Based on my what I've seen, they shouldn't have to field rookies so eager for quick results..."],["Leopold","Before that, Paloma, you need to explain the reason for attacking us."],["","Leopold interrupted Paloma's rambling."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","Just feels very..."],["Leopold","This time, no lying is allowed."],["Paloma","Hmm... do I really have to say it..."],["","Even with just the voice, Paloma's obvious hesitation and pause can be felt."],["Paloma","Because the Vice Captain is the traitor."],["","..."],["Paloma","Vice Captain, you sent the coordinates to Obsidian, didn't you?"],["Leopold","…Paloma, I won't defend myself, because everyone already reached a conclusion at the meeting earlier."],["Paloma","Ah… what a hassle. It would be great if there was a rule where lying meant death."],["Paloma","These half-hearted agreements made between humans are really useless…"],["Rosa","…Why would you make such a guess?"],["Paloma","Guess? It's not something half-hearted like that. Just like your sensing ability, I can perceive some things too…"],["Paloma","You see, unlike insignificant folks like us, if the Vice Captain is the traitor, then Obsidian is sure to win, right?"],["","Irrelevant logic, irrelevant emotions, she is merely imagining the worst outcome and striving to make her own efforts towards it."],["Paloma","So I want to give it a try... He's a traitor, so if I defect, he'll definitely support me, right?"],["Paloma","After all, communicating with me won't trigger any alarms. The two of us can work together here to capture Rosa, and the whole incident will inexplicably come to an end!"],["Rosa","..."],["Paloma","But what a pity... Is it because I'm usually so untrustworthy that even the Vice Captain is unwilling to cooperate with me?"],["Paloma","Or did you already see through my thoughts just now and chose to continue acting... That's truly impressive, Vice Captain, to be able to achieve such a level..."],["Rosa","I still don't understand why you keep making assumptions based on Leopold being a traitor."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","Don't you think it's more dangerous if no one believes such a thing is possible?"],["Paloma","Just like you, Rosa, have you ever imagined that things worse than death could happen to you?"],["Rosa","..."],["","She never thought about it, which is why she's in this situation now."],["Paloma","It's normal... not just you, even your partners couldn't believe it until they saw it with their own eyes..."],["Leopold","Enough, Paloma, if you didn't believe what was discussed in the meeting, you should have brought it up then."],["Leopold","If you keep making these suspicions, no one will be able to reach the truth."],["Paloma","Huh? I never said I didn't trust everyone, did I?"],["Paloma","Just think of it as a kind of insurance, a sort of... a little struggle because I don't have the authority to investigate."],["","Paloma's ST came to a halt, and the three arrived at an abandoned railway, which was no different from other abandoned facilities within the city."],["","If anything, it was even more desolate, with the surroundings eerily quiet, leaving only the rustling sound of sand brushing against the ST."],["Paloma","Talking about this nonsense, we arrived in no time... Let's get out of the STs."],["Paloma","The <yellow>evidence</yellow> I could gather is inside. It might be hard to accept at first, but rest assured..."],["Paloma","I will explain everything clearly."]],"561008101":[["","Entering the abandoned train, Rosa smelled a familiar scent."],["","A hint of pungent disinfectant, a touch of damp blood, and a whiff of decaying chemicals formed the scent of the laboratory."],["","A touch of darkness, a hint of death, coalescing into suffocating despair."],["","Paloma led the two through several carriages, turned back with a smile before the next door opened, and then pushed it open."],["","A dim fluorescent light, four operating tables, two buzzing instruments, and three dying bodies."],["","This is Paloma's temporary secret base, where she stayed when the leak occurred."],["Paloma","Come, now I have some questions for you..."],["","Paloma walks up to an operating table and speaks to the humanoid on it."],["Paloma","What organization are you?"],["Mobile Guard Officer","Obsidian Mobile Guard..."],["Paloma","Why are you here?"],["Mobile Guard Officer","To find... Rosa..."],["Paloma","How did you get information about Rosa?"],["Mobile Guard Officer","There's... there's a mole providing intel..."],["Paloma","Who's the mole?"],["Mobile Guard Officer","..."],["","Like a puppet, the guard under Paloma's control suddenly fell silent after obediently answering... Then, he began to tremble violently."],["","As if the puppet's spring had been wound too tightly, his joints started to creak, his muscles spasmed continuously, his head tilted to one side, and frothy blood trickled from the corner of his mouth."],["","Paloma stood aside with a frown, but there was no confusion in her expression, clearly knowing from the start that this would be the case."],["","She was simply dissatisfied with the outcome."],["","Before long, there was no sound from the operating table."],["Paloma","Although these guys are from headquarters, like the Predators, they've all undergone Rebirth technology Renovation with Disconnect Surgery to ensure stability."],["Paloma","Although both involve injecting arashi matter into the body as a form of Rebirth technology, unlike normal Predators, these guys had way too short of a testing phase..."],["","Paloma spread her arms wide, illustrating a length of time."],["Paloma","Let's say creating a normal Predator takes this much time, about two to three years..."],["","She lowered her arms and gestured with her right hand, pinching the air with a thumb and middle finger."],["Paloma","...But the time it took to create these guys? Two or three weeks tops."],["Rosa","So when you say defective products, you mean not the ones you created..."],["Paloma","The knowledge of Rebirth technology is something I've recently brushed up on from the Predators. From their rather traditional perspective, these spawned creatures are considered defective."],["Paloma","But from my personal viewpoint, the headquarters' approach is much more efficient... Let's put it this way, while the Predators are still observing and studying each individual, the headquarters has already started the production line."],["Paloma","With such a rapid infusion of arashi matter, they gain the same <yellow>battle power and vitality</yellow>, yet suffer far greater brain damage—yet that very damage makes them easier to operate and control than the Predators..."],["Leopold","But you shouldn't conduct such an experiment here, it violates..."],["Paloma","If we treat these as humans, it will be us who suffer."],["","Paloma walked up to a guard member, lifted his head, and directed Rosa and Leopold to look into his eyes."],["","Those eyes lacked something, and once Paloma mentioned the idea that the enemy was not human, Rosa quickly realized what the discordance was."],["","There was no soul within them."],["Paloma","If Predators are monsters capable of controlling their own arashi material, then these guys are merely puppets driven by arashi material."],["Paloma","Whether they are born like real humans through reproduction is still unknown..."],["Paloma","What if they are clones produced using technologies long banned by the convention?"],["Paloma","Besides the instructions above, they have no emotions, no will, not even... the capacity for madness."],["Paloma","Once they fall into enemy hands and are subjected to confidential interrogation or Renovation, they will immediately commit suicide... My God, I can't think of a more excellent tool than them."],["","Paloma carelessly tossed the body aside."],["Paloma","However, among us, you have the deepest understanding of this thing... Rosa, are you willing to believe that you were still human during the time you lost consciousness?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","I don't know, but that definitely wasn't me..."],["Paloma","At that time, you underwent a similar experiment. Even though your constitution is special and your affinity for arashi matter is unmatched, if that lunatic named Lucia continues to mess around for a while..."],["Paloma","You will end up looking like this."],["Rosa","..."],["","A tinge of fear swept through Rosa's heart; this is definitely a fate worse than death."],["Paloma","Before you came, I also tried hard, attempting to repair them using Rosa's method. It was the first time I felt both stupid and useless, so I changed direction..."],["Paloma","They are tough, and as long as I don't violate their initial instructions, I can maintain a certain degree of control."],["Leopold","But this has crossed the line, Paloma."],["","Paloma took out some tools and was about to demonstrate some results to the two when Leopold stopped her."],["Leopold","You've done well these past few years, so why now..."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","We've already cooperated with the Predators and been forced into this state of mutual suspicion, so why care about the means used?"],["Leopold","..."],["Paloma","And the more I understand the enemy, the more I doubt one thing... Leopold, even if you find the traitor, are you really confident that we can survive under these guys' hands with our base exposed?"],["Paloma","For now, we can still rely on guerrilla tactics to disperse their forces and attention. But if this continues, their numbers will grow, and they will swarm the entire city like locusts."],["Paloma","Imagine the sight of locusts devouring a field of grain... We are just helpless stalks of wheat among them. How can we stand against those ravenous teeth..."],["Leopold","Leave that decision to me."],["Paloma","Of course, of course, after all, you're the one who never makes mistakes, Leopold..."],["","Paloma deftly maneuvered around Leopold, reaching out to grasp the last team member's head. As if triggering some mechanism, the body began to tremble."],["Paloma","Tell me, was I fighting with you around here three hours ago?"],["Mobile Guard Officer","It's... it's you..."],["Paloma","Alright, you can die now."],["","After completing the Q&A, the body went limp."],["Paloma","Well, unlike us, these guys never lie, so they're my alibi."],["Rosa","No... that's just your side of the story."],["Rosa","Since you could manipulate them to attack us earlier, I have every reason to suspect this evidence is fabricated by you as well."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","Ah, now we're in a pickle... I never thought I'd make such a mistake..."],["Leopold","No need to rush to conclusions. First, go through the entire experience and find evidence that proves it happened."],["Paloma","Hmm... Is that so..."],["Paloma","Let me start by explaining why I'm here."],["Paloma","At first, I was at the checkpoint with Sapi, facing the enemy... Oh, and Sloth wasn't there from the beginning, so if he lies later, you should catch him."],["Paloma","I brought a lot of equipment with me when I came out, thinking I'd find a chance to slip away and set up a small base to capture some enemies for research... But Sapi kept an eye on me, not giving me a chance..."],["Leopold","If it's Sapientia, she would definitely keep a close eye on you... So how did you get here?"],["Paloma","About that..."]],"561009101":[["","Although they obtained the camera's memory card, lacking playback equipment, the three could only make the choice to crowd onto Paloma's ST to watch."],["","Amid Paloma's complaints about the crowd, this footage also proves her absolute innocence."],["","Although only her distant silhouette can be seen, the screen shows Paloma using this place as a base, constantly sniping, attracting enemies, incapacitating them, and recovering them."],["","At the end of the footage, when Paloma aimed at an enemy, she seemed to hesitate briefly, allowing the target to escape her snipe range and retreat the way it came."],["","Then the footage automatically shuts off, reflecting the thoughtful expressions of the three on the dark screen."],["Rosa","The last enemy escaped the way it came..."],["Paloma","...Ah! It was at that moment I got distracted by the alarm, which is why I let that guy get away..."],["Leopold","Based on the timestamp of the footage, Paloma has an indisputable alibi for when the leak happened."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","No matter how you look at it, being able to set up a trigger immune to an EMP—one that could start the STs and cameras—could only have been done by someone among us who knew the contingency plan in advance."],["Paloma","Phew... Although I don't know who caused the trouble, I really have to thank them."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","It's almost as if someone deliberately helped Paloma clear her of suspicion."],["Paloma","That's indeed the case, but what's wrong with that? Doesn't it give you one less suspect to worry about?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Maybe I'm overthinking it. If this is a trap you set yourself, then it's a perfectly forged piece of evidence..."],["Paloma","Then it must be truth!"],["Paloma","The truth, after all, is the most perfect evidence. The facts are laid out right in front of you, what is there to doubt?"],["Leopold","Even if this was arranged by Paloma herself, the outcome proves she is not involved with the leak."],["Leopold","In my opinion, the origin of these traps might be worth investigating, but there is no longer a need to continue pursuing Paloma."],["Rosa","But her deep connection with Obsidian and these secretive activities make it hard for me to believe she..."],["Paloma","Honestly... At this point, I feel that discussing motives won't convince anyone, but I still have to tell you, I have no contact with Obsidian anymore."],["Paloma","Whatever I do, it's to ensure this squad continues on, because this is my home."],["Paloma","Continuing to focus on me now is just a waste of time, allowing the real traitor to get closer to victory."],["","Though still maintaining a nonchalant demeanor, Paloma's eyes are fixed on Rosa, as if trying to convey something serious."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Is this all because of Sapientia?"],["Paloma","Huh? Why are you bringing up Sapi now..."],["Rosa","Anyone can sense there's something between you and her, and your previous suspicion about Leopold also gave me some insight..."],["Rosa","Now I have to ask you, if Sapientia is the traitor, what would you do?"],["","As if punishing Paloma's flippant attitude, Rosa asked this question."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","Heh... I never thought about that..."],["Paloma","If that really happend, then what we did in the past probably isn't much different to what you did."],["Rosa","Really...?"],["Leopold","Almost there, Rosa."],["Leopold","If our suspicions are not based on clues, then we have no right to stand where we are now."],["Rosa","...Sorry, Paloma, that's all the questions I wanted to ask."],["Paloma","No worries, no worries, I don't actually dislike arguing, it's just... now is really not the time for that."],["","The initial investigation ended rather abruptly."],["","Although Paloma's suspicion was cleared, the only ones left with the suspicion of being traitors are Veronica and Sloth, but the puzzles swirling in Rosa's mind have only increased."],["","Who set up the trap to lure Paloma here and then used the footage to prove her innocence... If it was the traitor, then what was the intention behind it..."],["","Simply using the method of elimination to find the traitor will ultimately lead to a dead end constructed by puzzles, with no way out."],["","That way, the truth will never be revealed."],["","Harboring doubts, Rosa and Leopold Ashford left Paloma's ST and headed towards their own STs separately, preparing for the next investigation."],["","Not far away, Paloma also got off her ST and hurriedly caught up to Rosa."],["","Leopold also paused slightly, turning back to look at the two, but from his position, he couldn't hear what Paloma was saying to Rosa."],["Rosa","Anything else?"],["Paloma","Here, catch."],["","A vial was quietly slipped into Rosa's hand."],["","Beneath the transparent glass tube wall was a colorless and crystal-clear liquid, and as soon as Rosa touched it, she sensed its components."],["Rosa","This is..."],["Paloma","The <yellow>Rebirth Serum</yellow>. It can be considered the latest achievement of the Rebirth experiment, but the one you have is just a trial version with reduced dosage."],["Paloma","This is a little gadget I replicated, allowing a normal person to temporarily possess the abilities of a Predator without losing memory."],["Paloma","This is the last one... but after using it once, the body will produce corresponding arashi antibodies, making it a once per lifetime kind of deal, so there's no point in making more."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Why give me something like this?"],["Paloma","Well, for starters, I gave everyone else a dose of this thing before. Although everyone was planning to keep it from you, it would be too unfair not to tell you in such a life-risking investigation."],["Paloma","But also... Rosa, I still don't believe you'll change."],["Paloma","In this squad, I'm the one who truly understands that nature is hard to change. In that regard, we're exactly the same..."],["Paloma","So I think, just like that Erinys you rejected, you'll end up using this thing sooner or later."],["Paloma","Since that's destined to be the outcome, why not make it more intense?"],["Rosa","No, I won't ever again..."],["","Rosa attempted to push the potion back into Paloma's hand, but it was forcefully stuffed into her pocket instead."],["","She then turned her head to look at Leopold, who was striding over, waved cheerfully, and greeted him loudly, using some words to brush him off."],["","In that moment, she also quietly gave Rosa her final advice."],["Paloma","That's right, we all fear situations worse than death."],["Paloma","But that's certainly not the worst; beyond that, there are things we are even more unwilling to face..."],["Paloma","<yellow>Choice</yellow> is something that never existed from the start."]],"561010101":[["Rosa","..."],["Leopold","What did Paloma say to you just now?"],["Rosa","Nothing much, just warning me again not to indulge in those useless doubts... with her unique sense of humor."],["Leopold","Really...?"],["","Rosa, piloting the ST, responded to Leopold casually, but couldn't help checking the vial in her arms."],["","Through the glass tube, she could feel the arashi matter flowing inside, dense yet gentle, with an incredible allure..."],["","When she was stopped by Paloma, she couldn't choose to confess to Leopold, so she had to continue hiding it afterwards."],["","Of course, she only considered it an important clue, rather than wanting to..."],["","..."],["Rosa","The next subject of investigation should be..."],["","As if deliberately trying to break the frozen topic and her own unease, Rosa posed a question to the voice channel."],["Leopold","It's Veronica. According to her position at the time, she should..."],["Sloth","Hey... Hey, hey... Can you hear me?"],["Sloth","This is Sloth. I'm in... the northern district of the Central Square. I've encountered a group of Obsidian guys here—can't handle it, need assistance."],["","Although this message was sent in the team channel, with only Rosa and Leopold able to move freely, it serves as a distress signal specifically for them."],["Rosa","Looks like it's time to..."],["Leopold","If the signal is from Sloth, it's not a serious situation. It can wait."],["Rosa","Meaning?"],["Leopold","During each mission where they split up, he would send out three to four distress signals. If you've worked with him long enough, you can discern the urgency of the situation from his tone."],["Leopold","Given the current situation... trust me, he can handle it himself."],["Rosa","Sounds like you trust him a lot."],["Leopold","Is that so... Haha..."],["","Responding to Rosa, Leopold couldn't help but laugh, as if it were some kind of funny joke."],["Leopold","If Sloth is a traitor, Rosa, from your current understanding of him, what reason would he have for betrayal?"],["Rosa","This is just my current speculation based on my observations. Considering his frequent evasive behavior, selling me out to Obsidian might give him the chance to leave the team under their protection and enjoy a comfortable life later on."],["Leopold","Is that so... If not for this situation, it wouldn't be out of the question for that guy..."],["Rosa","What do you mean...?"],["Leopold","How about this, during this break, let me tell you about Sloth's experiences?"],["Rosa","Understanding them better will aid in the investigation later... Please go ahead."],["Leopold","Let's start with the conditions for joining the Reversion Squad. It may seem like they're selecting some capable individuals, but in fact, the true purpose of this squad is... <yellow>punishment</yellow>."],["Rosa","<yellow>Punishment</yellow>, huh..."],["Leopold","This punishment is not aimed at anyone else, but at the members themselves."],["Leopold","All those who have made some big mistakes outside but still have some value are thrown in here to atone for their crimes... Most of the members before this batch didn't last until they could redeem themselves."],["Leopold","For example, Paloma's under scrutiny because of her dealings with Obsidian, Ada's UNCS background requires the strictest supervision. As for me, I had some conflicts with the military leadership... But Sloth..."],["Leopold","His mistake was... doing nothing."],["Rosa","It does... suit his personality."],["","Leopold is truly a master storyteller, instantly capturing people's interest."],["Leopold","During the war, he never followed a single order from his superiors, never actively participated in any battle, and was a somewhat popular <yellow>deserter</yellow> within the DLAF at the time."],["Leopold","The soldiers speculated about the reasons for his avoidance, initially thinking he was simply weak or cowardly."],["Leopold","But soon, everyone realized that not only did he escape, but anyone who stayed near him during missions invariably survived."],["Leopold","From being ridiculed at first, eventually everyone hoped to carry out missions with Sloth, so that mistakes would be blamed on the other party, and they could return alive to embrace their loved ones."],["Leopold","Sloth's unit, in an effort to keep the team stable, started separating him from the others and assigning him to carry out missions by himself, behind enemy lines..."],["Rosa","Since that's the case, why does the army continue to keep him?"],["","Rosa begins to recall the image of Sloth, yet that figure is so indistinct, as if in every moment of the past, he was merely an insignificant speck in the background."],["","In unnoticed corners, he even deliberately hid himself."],["Leopold","Because the military knew he had the capability."],["Leopold","Sloth's final outcome in the army was that all his former comrades died on the path of glory and commendation, while he unknowingly survived alone."],["Rosa","..."],["Leopold","Doing nothing may be acceptable for an individual, but for a soldier, especially in that era, it was an unforgivable mistake."],["Rosa","Just like us..."],["Leopold","After the war, he was sent to the Reversion Squad."],["","As he spoke, Leopold seemed to be lost in memories of the past, with a hint of joy unintentionally slipping into his voice, as if that emotion shouldn't quietly emerge at this moment, yet it was still hard to suppress."],["Leopold","At that time, I was the only one in the Reversion Squad, and Sloth was the second guy to join."],["Leopold","I took his order and asked him what he had done to deserve such punishment. This is how he answered..."],["Leopold","\"Punishment... Hmm... I heard there are fewer tasks here, isn't that a reward?\""],["Rosa","...Haha, that's quite an interesting response."],["Leopold","Interesting? This is quite a headache for me, it's a real hassle to assign him tasks..."],["Sloth","Hello? Hello? Vice Captain, you are on this channel, right?"],["Sloth","I'm really in trouble here, can you stop pretending not to hear now?"],["Rosa","How about it, Vice Captain? This is already his second call for help."],["","Due to the previous joke, Rosa's tone softened slightly, carrying a hint of teasing."],["Leopold","Don't worry, there will be a third distress signal soon... Before that, how about I finish the story?"],["Leopold","I told him that while the Reversion Squad might not have many routine tasks, every deployment means risking our lives. This is already the seventh time the squad has been formed..."],["Leopold","He listened to my intimidating stories while yawning, and summed it up at the end."],["Sloth","That's even better, it proves one thing... they've already given up hope on me."],["Sloth","Looks like in the end I won."]],"561010301":[["Sloth","This spot is good. We don't have to worry about Obsidian catching up for now..."],["","In a temporary safe house, Sloth glanced around. He was about to find another corner to sit in when he noticed the two people behind him were tracking his every move."],["Sloth","Oh right, you're here to investigate me, aren't you?"],["","He shrugged helplessly, pulled up a chair, and sat openly in front of the two, showing no signs of the tension of an impending interrogation."],["Rosa","Alright... Sloth, tell me, why weren't you on the front line during that operation?"],["Sloth","...It's simple, I just found a place to rest right after heading out."],["Leopold","Really...?"],["Sloth","Don't say it like that... Even though I was lazy, if Paloma hadn't left midway, that line could have held for a while longer, right?"],["Rosa","...Are you saying the responsibility isn't yours?"],["Sloth","You could say that, since I did mention from the start that I didn't want to go out."],["","His natural tendency to shirk responsibility made everyone ashamed, but Leopold was clearly accustomed to such conversations."],["Leopold","Then let's consider it a mistake in my personnel arrangement... So, Sloth, your choice of resting place was the Central Square, right?"],["Sloth","That's right, it's just near the west exit of the base, and shortly after we came out, I chose to set up camp there."],["Rosa","West exit... I see, no wonder you said at the time..."],["Rosa","I sensed the <yellow>sudden appearance</yellow> of enemies around the base periphery and sounded the alarm. Then Veronica ordered the attack, right?"],["Veronica","That's right, following Leopold's instructions, I discovered a wandering enemy at the west entrance of the base and destroyed it..."],["Sloth","That enemy..."],["Veronica","Do you have anything to confirm? The <yellow>wreckage</yellow> of the destroyed enemy still exists, you can go investigate."],["Sloth","No, it's nothing."],["Sloth","Do you remember what I said at the time... I was just about to talk about what happened then."],["Rosa","It's about Veronica's testimony... If there's a conflict between you two..."],["Sloth","No, everything she said is true."],["","Sloth interrupted Rosa's speculation, meticulously describing how Veronica appeared from the base and destroyed the ST."],["Leopold","That level of detail was never exchanged at the meeting... It seems you indeed witnessed it all firsthand."],["Sloth","If Veronica hadn't come, I was still wondering whether to deal with that enemy..."],["Rosa","But why didn't you testify at the meeting, so your suspicion..."],["Sloth","No, that still can't clear my suspicion."],["","Sloth remains in his lethargic state, slowly stating his unfavorable situation."],["Sloth","In fact, doesn't it make me even more suspicious?"],["Sloth","It's entirely possible that I used that enemy to lure out Veronica, then followed her all the way, sent the coordinates at the right time, and left, later disguising myself as if I had just arrived at the scene."],["Rosa","This possibility..."],["Leopold","Trying to track Veronica isn't that simple, and judging from the situation at the scene, you shouldn't have left the Central Square after that, but instead led the enemy to the Southern City, right?"],["Sloth","That's right, the facts are exactly as the Vice Captain said... But there's no absolute evidence to prove this fact, is there?"],["Rosa","But you should have brought it up for discussion at the meeting—why didn't you?"],["Sloth","Well, this..."],["","If both are possible, Rosa finds it hard to understand why the person in front of her would give up the chance to clear his name."],["","He seems to deliberately put himself in a position to be suspected, yet he doesn't care at all."],["Sloth","If I'm really cleared of suspicion, wouldn't I have to investigate with both of you?"],["Sloth","Just thinking about such a thing is unbearably troublesome..."],["Rosa","..."],["Leopold","This guy...!"],["Sloth","..."],["Sloth","Ah... I really don't get any of this..."],["","Sloth sighs, scratches his head, rises, and walks to the door, calling out to the two without looking back."],["Sloth","Hey, Rosa, weren't you the one saying we should suspect everyone back then... Giving up so soon?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Were you trying to keep evidence from the traitor during the meeting?"],["","The rules prohibit lying, but they don't prohibit withholding the truth."],["","The only reason Rosa can think of for Sloth risking his life was this: he holds evidence against the traitor and hopes to convey it to the investigator without the traitor knowing."],["Sloth","..."],["","Only silence responds to Rosa."],["","Like Paloma, Sloth is also testing the investigator."],["","If he were a traitor, there's no way he would've picked up on those clues..."],["Leopold","Sloth, are you sure you were at the Central Square the whole time?"],["Rosa","...!?"],["","Just an unintended reconfirmation, yet it clears Rosa's muddled mind, and the direction of progress becomes clear."],["Sloth","Didn't I already say... Although there's no evidence, the task I assigned myself at the time was to watch the entrance and see if any enemies approached."],["Rosa","If that's really the case... then Sloth, I have a question."],["Rosa","Since the entrance was already guarded, then where did the ST that Veronica destroyed come from?"]],"561011301":[["","He's still alive."],["","This was the good news they received when Sloth was dragged out of his ST—and it was the only good news."],["","In a rush to cover Rosa, he failed to adjust the position of his ST in time. The attack hit with near-perfect precision, directly into his cockpit..."],["Leopold","Hang in there, Sloth."],["Sloth","Cough... cough cough..."],["","He just moved from one pool of blood to another, with no sign of improvement in his condition."],["","The shrapnel from the blown-open cockpit hit his abdomen. Although it won't take his life immediately, given the current conditions..."],["Sloth","Rosa... is she alright?"],["Rosa","I'm here... you... you need to stay awake!"],["Rosa","We need to stop the bleeding first, we must..."],["","Rosa's two hands carefully avoided the massive steel fragment, yet the scene before her exceeded her expectations."],["Rosa","Damn... Damn...!"],["","Blood, like a spring, continuously gushed out, taking away the life of the person before her."],["Sloth","Ouch, that really stings..."],["Sloth","You two, don't worry, I know what I'm doing."],["Leopold","Stop, Sloth, keep breathing... don't talk!"],["Rosa","Leopold, we need to find some cloth for bandages, and if possible..."],["Sloth","Alright, alright, just listen to me first, okay..."],["","Sloth raises a hand, signaling everyone not to panic... weak, yet there's a sense of strength in it."],["Sloth","Rosa, even if you don't believe in yourself, it's okay."],["Rosa","What... what are you saying?"],["Sloth","Those who only rely on themselves will eventually lose trust in themselves due to failure. I can understand that feeling... I've been there..."],["Sloth","But trust in others is different, because trust in others is absolute and won't be diminished by failure."],["Sloth","And this trust, this feeling of having support behind you, is the basis for one's actions and judgments."],["","Sloth's hand is growing weaker... he doesn't have much time left."],["Sloth","The clues collected this time are not as fruitless as you think; they definitely mean something..."],["Sloth","I'm not doing this just to protect you. I simply believe in everyone, and in the you that everyone believes in..."],["Sloth","In the end, it can definitely be resolved... and alone, there's nothing that can't be done..."],["","Sloth's voice is barely audible, a whisper on the brink of death, yet it carries an unshakable resolve."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Don't speak, Sloth! Hold on, you can't fall here, you can't..."],["","Rosa's voice trembles slightly as a teammate falls before her, a sight she should be accustomed to by now."],["","But it was precisely this familiarity that reminded her of that hateful self... She couldn't protect everyone, just like she couldn't save her sister and those girls."],["Rosa","Once you're dead, belief means nothing..."],["Sloth","Is that so... that's something I never thought of... never..."],["Leopold","..."],["","Sloth's head slumped limply and slid down to the ground."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","No... No, no, there must be a way..."],["","At the moment when the shadows of the past overlapped with the current tragedy, Rosa felt the strange sensation in her arms."],["Rosa","Rebirth Serum... If it's the Predator's constitution..."],["","Rosa murmured, and as she suddenly realized and reached for the reagent in her arms, Leopold had already stepped forward, grabbing Sloth's shoulder in an attempt to pull him back from his drifting consciousness."],["Leopold","Sloth, where is the potion Paloma gave you!"],["Sloth","..."],["","With a slight movement of his fingers, Leopold understood the direction he indicated and found the vial of potion in the pocket on the side of Sloth's leg."],["","Then, without hesitation, he completed the emergency muscle injection."],["Rosa","Leopold, this is..."],["Leopold","Experimental Rebirth Serum, a creation by Paloma imitating the latest technology of Predator."],["Leopold","If everything goes smoothly, Sloth should now be able to..."],["","No, the problem isn't that, but rather..."],["","A strange sense of dissonance surged in Rosa's heart, yet she couldn't find any outlet for it."],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["Sloth","..."],["Sloth","*huff, huff*"],["","After what felt like an eternity, his faint breathing gradually became clearer, and the wound Rosa was covering stopped bleeding..."],["Rosa","It's just like the ST..."],["","Just like the ST's self-repair, Sloth's body gradually begins to heal itself."],["","In the world she perceives, the arashi material injected into Sloth's body is almost sentient, spontaneously gathering near the wounds, then beginning to merge... to reconstruct..."],["","And under the urging of her consciousness, this process can be even faster."],["","She tentatively reached out to grasp the fragment in her wound, then made up her mind and pulled it out."],["Sloth","Ugh... that really stings..."],["","In emergency care, removing an embedded object is generally a forbidden, as it can further worsen the bleeding."],["","But Rosa could see the efforts of the arashi material; under her command, the exposed wound only oozed a little more blood before it was sealed."],["Sloth","Sure enough... I never thought I would die, otherwise I would never have stuck my neck out like this..."],["Rosa","Incredible..."],["","Besides that, she didn't know what other exclamations she could make."],["","Sloth, who was about to go into shock from blood loss, has regained consciousness. Although still enfeebled, a hint of color has started to appear on his pale face."],["Leopold","Paloma said it can temporarily turn a normal person into a Predator... Sorry we kept it from you earlier."],["Sloth","So it can be used for this... Haha, I thought this thing only turned people into lunatics. I was going to throw it away without Paloma knowing."],["Leopold","I was just trying it out. According to Paloma's report, those top Predators have extraordinary self-healing abilities..."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","It seems the drug's effect has worn off..."],["","It seems that in order to repair this wound, the arashi material that could have lasted a while has almost completely disappeared."],["","But that's enough. Although Sloth's face is still pale as paper, he can now prop himself up on the floor and barely sit up."],["Sloth","Ah... After saying such words, I should've probably fainted. It's a bit embarrassing otherwise."],["Leopold","Heh, alright, since you can move again, we still have work to do..."],["Rosa","I can feel the enemies outside gathering again. If there are new reinforcements, Leopold's device won't hold for long."],["Sloth","Do we still have to find a way to break through? In my current state, I'm afraid..."],["Leopold","Our reinforcements should be arriving soon..."],["","Just as Leopold finished speaking, a familiar voice echoed in the trio's earpieces."],["Veronica","Veronica has arrived at the Central Square."],["Veronica","Where's the one seeking reinforcements? Come out quickly, don't keep me waiting too long!"]],"561012101":[["","Stall for time."],["Veronica","That's the only possibility..."],["","Veronica paced back and forth in the temporary safe house in the south of the city, her brow furrowed, with each heel striking the ground echoing hollowly."],["","She continued speaking, words as hollow as the echoes."],["Veronica","One of the two tracked me using some method, then sent the coordinates at the right time, escaping the scene while I was surrounded by enemies..."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Is that really the case?"],["","She knew very well that this was just a stalling tactic."],["Veronica","Following this logic, that Sloth guy is the most suspicious. After I dealt with the enemies in the Central Square, he led the enemies to the Southern City, making me engage them..."],["Veronica","He can track my location, so he can naturally rack up tracking and framing... But can he simultaneously complete the task of guiding the enemies? Why didn't Rosa sense new enemies?"],["","But even delaying time has its significance."],["Veronica","If there was prior collusion and the enemies cooperated with his actions, then it could naturally be established... But the problem is, in this incident, everyone only had one chance to send information."],["Veronica","In other words, before the leak occurred, everyone should be considered an enemy in the eyes of Obsidian."],["Veronica","Therefore, Sloth being a traitor is unlikely."],["","As long as there is time, no matter how desperate the situation, there is a possibility of breaking through."],["Veronica","So what about Paloma? She was located in the suburban area on the west side, where there were no signs of Obsidian STs. She had ample time and space to sneak around."],["Veronica","But unlike Sloth, how could she manage to know my location in advance and track me?"],["","This is a common thought among people, which is why countless individuals, when faced with certain death, resort to extremely disgraceful ways to stall for useless time..."],["","They are just hoping for a miracle to happen, without knowing how a miracle can come to pass."],["Veronica","Did she have the chance to place a tracking device on my ST? Impossible. I've taken all measures to prevent tracking, and the tracking signal would also be disrupted by the aftermath of the EMP, rendering it ineffective."],["Veronica","Did she ambush me on my inevitable path? This is a feasible plan, but how was it accomplished... By what means could she predict my temporary route in advance..."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Enough, this kind of reasoning is far too disgraceful..."],["","If the wrong direction is chosen, all struggles are meaningless. People need to understand this."],["","And Veronica understands this."],["Veronica","It's impossible to keep up with my high mobility without being discovered by me and the Obsidian people."],["Veronica","Predicting my route in advance and ambushing me on it is also impossible for a plan that requires precise operation."],["Veronica","I shouldn't be thinking about how to turn the impossible into possible; that's just overthinking."],["Veronica","Think again about the absolute clues that can serve as a starting point for reasoning... that is..."],["","I can't expect help from others now; the only one I can trust is myself..."],["Veronica","I am definitely not a traitor."],["","This may still be the wrong path."],["Veronica","But... will anyone believe it?"],["","But she has no choice."]],"561014101":[["","So cramped."],["","Even with all the complex emotions rushing through her mind, this was Rosa's main feeling after boarding the rear seat of Veronica's ST."],["","Physical discomfort once again triumphed over psychological unease."],["Veronica","How does it feel sitting in the back?"],["Rosa","A bit cramped..."],["Veronica","Really? Could you be a bit less slim than I imagined?"],["Rosa","..."],["Veronica","Just a joke... Although I haven't experienced sitting in the back, the machinist who debugged it told me it was designed according to the cockpit's proportions."],["Rosa","Cockpit proportions, huh..."],["","While people often describe the cockpit as the pilot's steel cage, if they experience Rosa's current seat, they might reconsider their metaphor."],["","This rear seat is basically a \"tiger cage\" within a prison; just sitting in it occupies all the space, making it difficult to stand up or raise your hands."],["Veronica","I can see all your indices here, but if you feel any discomfort, please let me know immediately."],["Rosa","If it's just this stretch of road, there shouldn't be any problem."],["Veronica","Alright."],["","After speaking, a brief silence fell between them."],["","Since Veronica arrived in the city and got involved in this incident, Rosa has only had one one-on-one conversation with her... and the result was far from harmonious."],["","The \"Arrogant Valkyrie,\" unable to understand the struggles of ordinary people—this was Veronica's assessment of Rosa at the time."],["Veronica","Rosa, regarding the investigation you conducted earlier..."],["Rosa","..."],["Veronica","Sorry, according to the rules, I shouldn't be asking you these questions right now."],["","Before Rosa could respond, Veronica had already interrupted and dismissed her own inquiry."],["","Unlike before when she kept asking questions, now she seems very cautious. Even without stuffing a cloth into her mouth, she would stop herself."],["Rosa","It's okay... Soon, we will share all the findings of the investigation with everyone."],["Veronica","...But at the very least, I want to know why you believe in me."],["Veronica","Did you judge that I'm not a traitor, or did you decide that even if I were a traitor, I wouldn't choose to reveal my identity now?"],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Some things are still in the speculative stage for me, so... I'm sorry."],["Veronica","I see... So we can at least say your trust has some rational basis, can't we?"],["Rosa","Huh?"],["Veronica","That's fine then..."],["","A sense of relief."],["","Even communicating only through the microphone, even trying to hide it, Rosa can still sense Veronica's emotions at this moment."],["","Rosa's trust seems to bring her an indescribable burden, but after confirming it, she finds relief."],["Veronica","I'm sorry for what happened before..."],["Rosa","...?"],["Veronica","It's about... about what I said, that you're arrogant and not a qualified sister... I went too far... The arrogant one was me."],["Rosa","It's all in the past, you don't need to dwell on it."],["","How could she not? Just thinking about Rosa still brought a pang to her heart."],["","But compared to the beginning, it was already much better... Amazing, considering only half a day had passed."],["Veronica","Don't dwell on it, she says... Hah. If only—that kind of person must sail through life without a care in the world."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","Maybe so..."],["","While engaging in this conversation, Veronica continues to pilot the ST through the city, breaking through one enemy after another."],["","The spare seat is also equipped with a monitor, and through the screen, Rosa's heart is filled with admiration for her skills."],["","Having lost her Hyper-Aptamer combat abilities, Rosa had become an ordinary pilot. From this equal footing, she can better understand the strengths of other pilots."],["","It's a truth forever beyond the grasp of someone who used to rely solely on her innate gifts: the battle power that humans can achieve only after countless trials and refinement."],["Veronica","By the way, did Leopold ever tell you why he was transferred to the Reversion Squad?"],["Rosa","He talked to me about others, but when it comes to his own matters..."],["Veronica","Honestly, he's just how he used to be... Unless you chase him for answers, don't expect to hear him talk about himself."],["Rosa","...Do you know him well?"],["Veronica","I don't know how he's doing in the Reversion Squad, but before that... well, I know a few things about him."],["Veronica","After all, in the past, I was one of his subordinates."],["Rosa","So that's why when we ran into each other before..."],["Veronica","\"Before making a decision, think about your teammates!\""],["","With an uncharacteristic hint of humor, Veronica suddenly mimicked Leopold's tone. Coming from her, it came as quite a surprise."],["Rosa","..."],["Veronica","What, not even a smile?"],["Rosa","No, I just didn't expect you to..."],["Veronica","It doesn't sound like something I'd say... because I have no right to say it."],["","Her voice remained steady."],["Veronica","Leopold is an almost perfect commander. Under his command, my team completed numerous missions during the counterattack phase, achieving the nearly impossible feat of zero casualties."],["Veronica","When you put it that way, he seems capable of anything, but in reality, what he does is quite simple. He just considers all factors comprehensively and makes a judgment on whether the task can be completed."],["Veronica","For things that cannot be done, he will choose to give up, and this is his promise to his \"teammate\"."],["","This is exactly the same as Sapientia's evaluation of Leopold."],["","From the past to the present, he has remained unchanged."],["Veronica","But misfortune... such a thing is truly terrifying, even Leopold cannot predict where it might be hiding."],["Veronica","On the return trip of that final task, I encountered a variable that no one could predict..."],["Rosa","..."],["","In the depths of her mind, Rosa already sensed what Veronica was about to say."],["","She also understood why Veronica harbored such deep malice towards her from the very beginning."],["Veronica","That's you, Rosa, the UNCS Valkyrie."],["Rosa","I..."],["Veronica","Don't bother thinking back. We were just a nameless squad with no reason to stick in your mind."],["Veronica","If you pretend to recall and repent, that would truly disgust me."],["Rosa","...Sorry."],["","So she could only offer an apology without any weight."],["Veronica","Although I've heard about your performance from others... it was only when facing you that I understood the meaning of those legends."],["Veronica","In my eyes, at that time... rather than being like an ace pilot, you were more like a... natural disaster."],["Veronica","Trying to defeat you is like dreaming of stilling an earthquake or taming lightning. Under Leopold's remote command, we immediately began to scatter and flee."],["Veronica","\"Do your best to stay alive!\""],["Veronica","This was Leopold's instruction to us, but I did not follow the order."],["Veronica","I shot at you."],["","In that moment, firing a weapon—that act of aggression—was actually an act of kindness."],["","Faced with the force of a natural disaster, it was not really an attack, but a way of protecting others."],["Veronica","I wanted to attract your attention so that my teammate could survive."],["Veronica","But when you dodged the attack and pointed the gun at me, it was my teammate who pushed me away and took the hit."],["Veronica","And then, the real disaster struck..."],["","She may have not wanted to hear it, but Veronica's voice went on, echoing through the headphones."],["Veronica","The allies who were in the middle of retreat all turned around—and aimed their guns at you."],["","Her voice recounted that moment—how the hope of survival flowed through gunfire, passed from one person to the next, yet no one was willing to reach out and take it."],["","\"Sacrifice\"—this hysteria continuously encroached upon the team, turning what could have been a tolerable misfortunate into a complete tragedy."],["","Natural disasters are not swayed by such spirit, or perhaps... because this was a battlefield, she simply didn't notice."],["","They were just a group of overconfident challengers, easily defeated and swept away by her."],["","Until the very last one."],["","Like a cruel joke of fate, this person was the one who triggered the disaster."],["","Then, perhaps due to an order or a more urgent task deadline, the calamity suddenly left the battlefield, hastily putting an end to the tragedy."],["Veronica","Rosa, do you know?"],["Veronica","Sometimes, sacrifice does not bring hope, but rather a curse left by the dead for the living."],["Veronica","Shortly after that, Leopold was transferred from his post, and I left the army to join the Oversight Committee."],["Veronica","Because I heard that there, cooperation with others was not required, and most inspectors act alone—which suits me fine."],["","The tragedy never really ended. It kept unfolding, one point after another, until it reached Rosa's eyes."],["Rosa","..."],["Rosa","I know, this is all my..."],["Veronica","No, you don't understand... I'm not blaming you for this."],["Veronica","Even if it wasn't that great war, what we experienced was still war. None of us were any better or worse than the other; we were all just caught up in it, carrying out our so-called missions."],["Veronica","Blaming all the resentment on you would be no different from running away."],["Rosa","..."],["","Silence crept back into the narrow pilot's cabin. The one once known as \"Calamity\" tried to speak, but she couldn't find a single word of comfort to offer."],["","But even so, she still wants to know where Veronica's initial resentment came from. She wants to understand this, she wants..."],["","To apologize to everyone she has hurt."],["","After this thought emerged, she finally understood what the truth behind it was."],["Rosa","I won't act recklessly, Veronica."],["Veronica","...But Rosa, can people really change?"],["Veronica","I know my nature, so I devoted myself to this position that doesn't allow trusting anyone or forming bonds with anyone, binding myself."],["Veronica","But eventually, you will return to your teammates, and... you will surely encounter panic and dilemmas again."],["Veronica","At that time, can you still ensure that you will think rationally and make reasonable judgments like you do now?"],["Veronica","And not avoid, not actively sacrifice, thereby passing on sadness and self-blame?"],["Rosa","I..."],["Veronica","Before making a decision, can you consider the feelings of your teammates?"],["Rosa","..."],["","Did she consider the feelings of her teammates?"],["","This question is so critical. Did the Valkyries of the UNCS ever have \"teammates\"?"],["","No, if you include those people... those she wants to save..."],["","Ada, Sylvie, that mercenary... and countless teammates, did you ever consider their feelings before making the choice to sacrifice yourself?"],["Veronica","If you only want to atone, nothing will change, Rosa."],["Rosa","..."],["Veronica","A sacrifice made without consent brings only curses in its wake."],["Veronica","In the worst case, this curse will spread."],["Veronica","And you are the beginning of it all. The curse you bring will affect everyone on this island..."],["","Am I... Cursing my teammates?"],["","With a noble and indisputable sacrifice, gain the right to eternal rest, leaving teammates to continue struggling and surviving in the world."],["","Was the so-called reason in the past actually a form of escape?"],["","Was that chaotic and dark time truly the right choice?"],["","..."],["","Even more unexpectedly, the battle described by Veronica suddenly surfaced in her mind, drawing her further into the abyss."],["","The one who first opened fire on her—and ultimately survived—now stood before her."],["","She has never forgotten those mistakes."],["","And now, what should I do to make it right?"],["Rosa","I..."],["Veronica","Rosa? What's wrong?"],["Rosa","What happened..."],["Veronica","You've been acting strange since just now..."],["","Veronica's voice pulled Rosa out of her daze. The throbbing pain in her head made it clear that this—right now—was reality."],["","Is this the lingering effect of the experiment...? Then from what point did the Veronica I was talking to just now become a hallucination?"],["Rosa","I'm fine... Veronica, I have something to give you."],["","But even if it was an illusion, Rosa made a decision at this moment."],["Veronica","What is this..."],["","Through a small opening between two seats, Veronica obtained a transparent vial with no labels or markings."],["","Like Veronica, this is how Rosa binds herself."],["Rosa","The trial version of the Rebirth Serum is a potion developed in collaboration between Paloma and Predator, temporarily granting the abilities of Predator, thereby boosting the resonance and vitality of ST."],["Rosa","For a normal person, it wouldn't leave any side effects, but for me, all effects are unknown."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Rosa, I'm glad you weren't affected by Sapientia, otherwise this incident would have been a complete defeat for us."],["Rosa","Sapientia isn't wrong, it's just..."],["Veronica","I understand, but what we need more now is the current you."],["Veronica","If your trust in me is baseless, I would only feel fear, reminding me of everything that happened... That's definitely not a good direction..."],["Veronica","But this feeling of being trusted, I really do miss it... Thanks."],["Rosa","...I need to thank you too."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Come on, responding with thanks at a time like this, have you thought about how I should reply?"],["","Veronica returned to her initial bad mood, but it no longer felt so annoying."],["Veronica","I have a piece of intel now... Rosa, confirm once again, are you sure you have evidence that makes me trustworthy?"],["Rosa","Huh?"],["Veronica","Really... what am I even asking? Besides you right now, is there anyone else I can trust..."],["","Veronica took a deep breath and then confessed to Rosa."],["Veronica","Rosa, I am the traitor."],["Veronica","The coordinate signal was sent from my ST."]],"561018101":[["","As soon as Sapientia finished speaking, everyone turned their gaze to Leopold."],["","No further arguments, no further accusations. Next, it's time to vote with actions."],["","Standing near Leopold Ashford, Sloth draws his gun, turns and levels it. However, just as he is about to pull the trigger, Leopold seizes the muzzle, grabbing it firmly in his hand."],["","Bang!"],["","The first bullet grazes past, sparking a tiny flash in the corner of the room."],["","Sloth makes a quick decision. He lets go and delivers a heavy punch directly at Leopold's face. But Leopold anticipated the attack. He grabs Sloth's arms and pulls forcefully, causing Sloth to stumble forward—straight into a counter-punch."],["","The fist solidly strikes Sloth's abdomen, hitting his old, unhealed wound. The intense pain instantly brings him to the ground."],["","The moment Leopold lets go, Veronica is already in front of him. She moves swiftly, bracing her hand on the table and leaping up. Concentrating all her strength in her knee, she strikes Leopold squarely in the face."],["","However, the difference in physique between the two prevents the blow from completely knocking him down. Leopold Ashford merely covers his face, staggering back a few steps, then grabs a nearby chair and hurls it at her with force."],["","Veronica quickly raised her hand to block and steady herself. As she was preparing to attack again, Leopold Ashford seized the opportunity to dash to the side, burst through the door, and swiftly escaped from the monitoring room."],["Paloma","Wow... that looks painful..."],["Paloma","As expected, when it comes to this kind of thing, neither us lab rats nor that invalid are any good at all."],["Veronica","Damn, he got away."],["Sapientia","...Sloth, are you okay!"],["Sloth","*cough, cough...* Now that's gonna leave a bruise... But I'll live, just gimme a moment..."],["Veronica","Hey! Isn't it time to stop standing around?"],["Rosa","..."],["","Veronica's call reawakened Rosa, who seemed to be in a daze since Sapientia stood to testify."],["","Like a sudden jolt, a resolute expression returned to her eyes."],["Rosa","This isn't the time to consider such matters... Sapientia, is there a way to seal all the entrances and exits in the base?"],["Sapientia","No, the Vice Captain has higher management authority than I do... but I'll do my best to slow down his escape."],["Rosa","That's it... Everyone, we must keep Leopold under control in the base and prevent him from contacting the Obsidian troops outside."],["Rosa","If everything goes well, this will be the final battle!"]],"561019101":[["","It's over."],["","Leopold's ST had been shut down, and after the battering he took in combat, he was in no condition to put up much resistance when they dragged him from the cockpit."],["","But at this moment, he remained silent, no longer as excited as before, allowing Veronica to handcuff him and push him into a room for imprisonment."],["","In the room, everyone began discussing ways to counter the Obsidian attack, but they vaguely sensed something unusual..."],["","They had already spent a lot of time capturing Leopold, so why hasn't the Obsidian attack arrived yet?"],["","Is it really all over?"],["","As such a significant event comes to a close, Rosa still doesn't feel that sense of relief... Everything in her mind is still shrouded in a veil, unable to break free..."],["","The gradually rising sense of dissonance makes it unbearable for her."],["Rosa","Leopold, can you answer one more question for me?"],["","Rosa leaned down, facing Leopold who was tied up in the corner, and asked a question."],["Leopold","..."],["Rosa","There's no doubt that you are the one who sent the coordinates, but... why do you always deliberately guide me to discover the truth?"],["Leopold","...That's just your illusion."],["Rosa","No... all those crucial clues, they were all..."],["Paloma","It seems like you were the one who said you wanted to investigate those puppets... Wait, I think I understand..."],["Paloma","Heh, it must be the Vice Captain's conscience kicking in, hoping that you, Rosa, would expose him here."],["Paloma","\"Although I've been corrupted by the DL higher-ups, I still... wish someone could stop me!\""],["Paloma","That's probably the feeling..."],["Rosa","...No, I don't think Leopold is that kind of person."],["Rosa","Even though this has happened, I still want to... believe in him now."],["","Funnily enough, the one who first emphasized the importance of trust to her was this traitor."],["","Ignoring Paloma's winking and gesturing beside her, Rosa continued to stare at Leopold Ashford, hoping to find something in his calm eyes."],["Veronica","I agree... Leopold wouldn't be the kind of guy to do things halfway. If he is determined to go against us, he wouldn't make these mistakes."],["Leopold","Heh... But conspiracies always have a little slip-up somewhere, don't they?"],["Rosa","As long as it's not discovered, it's not a slip-up... You were guiding me to find those oversights."],["Leopold","..."],["Veronica","Asking him now would be a waste of time... Leave it to me after we leave here."],["Rosa","But..."],["Paloma","Ah, Rosa, can't you just take a break?"],["","Although Paloma is as offbeat as usual, for some reason, Rosa couldn't shake the feeling that she was intentionally obstructing her."],["","It's a bit strange..."],["Sapientia","Paloma, let's leave this to them..."],["Paloma","Unlike Sapi, who's a homebody, Rosa has been quite busy with many things along the way, even though she's a patient..."],["","The familiar sound of playful banter between the two rings out, Veronica stands with her hands on her hips and a frown, attempting to mediate. Meanwhile, Sloth, as usual, rests with closed eyes in the corner."],["","That's right, it's all over. The traitor has been exposed, and now it's time to return to normalcy."],["","But just like the meticulous reasoning before, through that unfathomable intuition, one can predict that the unexpected is about to happen."],["","At this moment, a static noise comes through the headphones."],["???","Hey... Hey, hey..."],["???","You... guys in the base..."],["Rosa","...!"],["Veronica","A transmission from Morgana... Reinforcements are on their way!"],["Morgana","This is Morgana, reinforcements are already on the way..."],["Morgana","There's also an urgent message. On the way here, I learned that someone leaked the coordinates to the enemy."],["Sapientia","..."],["Morgana","Of course, I believe you already noticed this, but judging from the signal source..."],["Morgana","The device that leaked the coordinates is likely not the same as the one that leaked the city coordinates earlier."],["","......"],["","So, is there a possibility of two informants?"],["","So... everything previously deduced is..."],["","Time seems to stretch into eternity at this moment."],["Rosa","Leopold! Is there another trai..."],["","Rosa quickly turned and questioned Leopold, but before she could finish, she followed Leopold's surprised gaze to see another dangerous signal."],["","Or rather, she was the embodiment of danger."],["Paloma","What a pity..."],["Sapientia","Paloma! Don't..."],["","Paloma forms her hand into the shape of a gun, aiming at Rosa."],["","Then, as if she suddenly thought of something, she turns the muzzle towards her own temple, smiling."],["","Just as Sapientia's gasp escapes, her hand has already pulled the nonexistent trigger."],["Veronica","Rosa, get down!!!"],["","Veronica lunges at Rosa, who hasn't reacted yet, and before they hit the ground, Paloma's lips tremble slightly."],["Paloma","*Pop!*"],["","Boom!!!"],["","A jolt. A booming roar."],["","In an instant, everything before her eyes spins violently. When she regained her senses, all that remained was wreckage."],["Rosa","Hmm... what on earth..."],["","Turning to look, it's the eerie barrel of Paloma's ST. Just now, she remotely controlled her ST through her own intelligence framework."],["","That crazy girl sniped the room with her ST's rifle!"],["Paloma","Haha... hahaha..."],["Paloma","Ahhahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha..."],["Paloma","Ahhahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha!!!"],["","Amidst the room's wreckage, Paloma was alone, chuckling to herself."],["","As if following her laughter, the ST put away its sniper rifle and stepped forward towards the crowd."],["Paloma","Leopold... Sapi... Hellooo... can anyone still hear me?"],["Paloma","Oh no, I didn't expect that. This is getting interesting..."],["","The explosion's impact still rattled her mind as Rosa raised her head. Her sight blurred and doubled, yet she could still make out the vivid pink hair—its owner was the first to rise."],["","Children can be strangely cruel."],["","Even in a normal family, living a normal life, some children will still skin animals or stuff firecrackers into living creatures and enjoy it. These are unique interests of children that adults cannot comprehend."],["","When they grow up, most of these children slip into society, inside and out appearing no different from anyone else. But a few... they never let go of that so-called \"childlike heart.\""],["","Just like the one in front of us."],["","For some reason, Paloma's voice doesn't convey any madness, only a pure, childlike joy."],["Paloma","I'm the one who betrayed you from the very beginning... Well? Showing up like this at the moment of revelation—quite the twist, don't you think?"],["Paloma","It's just like the surprise of finding some ice cream at the bottom of the cone after finishing the top and chewing on the cone to pass the time."],["","Paloma's figure staggered, yet her voice remained vibrant. This eerie vitality makes one wonder if she possesses the abilities of a Predator."],["","Paloma walks over to Leopold, pressing her foot against his neck, and pauses for a moment."],["","She is feeling his pulse."],["Paloma","Sigh... Still alive? That's really unexpected..."],["Paloma","I really don't understand what the Vice Captain was thinking, sending coordinates on his own, getting exposed..."],["Paloma","If you'd held on a little longer and kep stalling, even Rosa wouldn't have figured it out... But this turn of events is okay too—so I'll be taking you with me!"],["Paloma","If I just let the mystery continue like this, I wouldn't even get my chance to make an appearance, would I?"],["","Paloma's ST arrived at the scene. Paloma boarded the ST and placed the unconscious Leopold into the cockpit."],["","Although it's a bit crowded, it's okay for short-time piloting."],["","Just then, the others began to move... The first to stand up was that shade of blue."],["Sapientia","Pa... Paloma! Please, don't do this anymore..."],["Paloma","Huh? Sapi, what do you want me not to do?"],["Sapientia","Clearly... this isn't you..."],["Paloma","Strange, but this is just the way I am."],["","As Sapientia, unsteady on her feet, still tried to approach her, Paloma stuck out her tongue with a smile."],["Paloma","Don't try to catch up, Sapi."],["Sapientia","..."],["","With that, the cockpit door closed, and Paloma left the place with Leopold."],["","Everyone stood up, and the next target was self-evident."],["Rosa","Sapientia, we must catch up to Paloma... Are you okay?"],["Sapientia","Huh?"],["","The things everyone worried about didn't happen. Sapientia showed almost no signs of despair and made a decision in an instant."],["","As if... she knew this would happen all along and was prepared."],["Sapientia","She can't be allowed to continue making mistakes."]],"561021101":[["","..."],["","What happened?"],["","Why can't I see anything?"],["","Was it that dream again? Did I go back?"],["","No... It's not a dream..."],["","Struggling to breathe, all that fills my mouth and nose is dust."],["","Trying to struggle, the pain gradually encroaches on my limbs."],["","I see... I was buried... but why?"],["","Hasn't everything already ended?"],["","Ah... it seems like things around me are starting to loosen..."],["","Who... is someone going to take me out of here?"],["","After regaining light, all I see is a field of ruins."],["","The underground base is half-ruined, with steel beams and concrete blocks from the ceiling hanging in mid-air, smoke billowing everywhere. The red emergency lights flicker weakly, casting shadows all around."],["","And the one who dug himself out from the building debris is Sloth, piloting his ST... Or rather, it was because he used his ST to block the falling debris at the moment of the collapse that everyone was able to survive."],["","It seems I am the last one to be rescued. Concerned gazes are all focused on me."],["Sloth","Alright, I dug her out."],["Rosa","Cough... cough cough..."],["Veronica","Rosa, are you alright...?"],["Rosa","I... I'm fine... What happened? Why did it suddenly..."],["Sapientia","It's... it's Obsidian... They've found us..."],["Leopold","Calm down, those dogs haven't found us yet, but... it's only a matter of time."],["Leopold","They've realized the coordinates were fake and lost direction due to our previous maneuvering, so this is the tactic they've resorted to. How pathetic..."],["Veronica","So how did they find us?"],["Leopold","They didn't find us, they just guessed the base was underground, so they used larger-scale munitions to bomb the entire city."],["Leopold","Including weapons like bunker buster bombs attacking suspicious areas, trying to find our location by flipping the entire city... Should we call it madness or fearlessness?"],["","Due to the damage to the buildings, the sound of explosions on the surface gradually reached everyone's ears, heralding the arrival of the enemy."],["Veronica","How is it possible, such large-scale military bombing, the alliance must..."],["Leopold","They're gambling."],["Leopold","They're betting that due to the city's special relationship, it won't be discovered by other forces in a short time. This also proves one thing... Rosa's value is worth their all-out effort at the table."],["Paloma","...Do you have any plans to deal with this situation?"],["Leopold","Plans... Well... It's not like I don't have any..."],["","In this extreme situation, Leopold smiled."],["Leopold","Since we've forced the enemy to this extent, it proves that what we did before was correct. We just need to keep going."],["Veronica","Keep going... Does that mean we continue to run?"],["Leopold","No, they've definitely discovered the existence of this base. If we escape now, we'll only be driven into their encirclement..."],["Rosa","Just running away won't lead to victory."],["Veronica","Rosa..."],["Leopold","That's right... Next, we'll have to start a frontal battle."],["Sapientia","No... To defeat them head-on, such a thing is simply..."],["Leopold","Victory isn't necessary. Reinforcements are already on the way... I can tell that Morgana is also the type who only acts when she's confident..."],["Leopold","I trust her, so as long as we hold on, we have a chance to win."],["Sapientia","..."],["Paloma","Alright, alright, Sapi, since we've already made a decision, don't mutter annoying things here."],["Paloma","The battle is about to begin—let's go help everyone get their STs ready first."],["","Saying this, Paloma pulled the somewhat disoriented Sapientia away from the discussion, searching for remaining equipment and repairing the damage left by the previous battle."],["Veronica","Leopold, just talking about trust... that's not like a decision you would make."],["Leopold","Is that so? After all, I haven't finished explaining my plan..."],["Leopold","Veronica, you're responsible for taking Rosa and escaping... If we delay here, you can hold out until reinforcements arrive."],["Rosa","No..."],["Leopold","Enough, this is not a game of suspicion and schemes... Veronica, what are you standing there for! Take her away!"],["Veronica","..."],["","Faced with Leopold's reprimand, Veronica remained unmoved and firmly stood by Rosa's side."],["Rosa","I will also participate in the battle."],["Leopold","You know what happens when you get into that ST... You're just thinking of taking everything on yourself again. How is this any different from the past..."],["Rosa","It's different, Leopold."],["Leopold","What's different? Damn it! I thought you really changed..."],["","Leopold reached up and scratched his head in frustration, his usual calm demeanor starting to slip away."],["","This isn't like the previous facade, the pretense, but genuine anxiety."],["Leopold","You know? Everything you do, Ada sees it all. Although I raised her, that girl... has always looked up to you as a role model."],["Leopold","Relying on innate power, just like you did back then, always wanting to handle everything alone, because..."],["Leopold","You are her real sister, Valkyrie."],["Rosa","..."],["Leopold","She can't keep winning forever, and you know what this mindset will ultimately lead to... So, you must survive, you must tell her that this is all wrong."],["Leopold","Of course, her temper might be even more stubborn than you imagine now, and she won't listen to you, but at least with you around, she has no reason to continue."],["Leopold","And if you leave here once again, everything will..."],["","A person's eyes tell the story of their life."],["","Especially the current mood, which is printed in the largest bold type."],["","From Leopold's eyes, Rosa saw fear."],["Leopold","If we sacrifice, then it's understandable, it's all part of the mission, but..."],["Rosa","Leopold, losing power and spending time with you all has taught me many things... This might be the first time I've learned how to trust and rely on others."],["Rosa","I will also teach this to Ada."],["Leopold","..."],["Veronica","Haha... Truly impressive, Valkyrie."],["","As Leopold was stunned by Rosa's words, Veronica laughed."],["","She took out the potion from her bosom and handed it to Rosa."],["Veronica","You need it more than I do now."],["Rosa","Hmm."],["","Without the previous hesitation and fear, Rosa injected the potion into herself after receiving it."],["Leopold","Rebirth Serum... Veronica, what are you doing?"],["Veronica","Don't get me wrong... Leopold, I'm more afraid than you that someone might die because of me again, but..."],["Veronica","Rosa, you wouldn't do that, would you?"],["Rosa","Of course... I won't slip away without a farewell again."],["Paloma","Hey! Rosa, we brought it to you!"],["","A familiar feeling is approaching, and the gradually rising resonance in her heart lets Rosa know what Paloma has brought her, even without turning around."],["","Without a trace of fear, facing the upcoming battles and challenges, her heart is filled only with a burning fighting spirit."],["","Turning around, the Erinys stands tall before her."],["","This teammate, renovated three times, is also responding to her expectations."],["Paloma","And take this one too."],["","Paloma, lying on top of the ST, dropped a package. Upon opening it, there were neatly stacked black combat uniforms."],["Paloma","I made some modifications when I had some free time earlier. Hmm... the amplification effect should be better now."],["Rosa","Thanks, Paloma."],["Leopold","Paloma, you are the one who knows best what the result of Rosa doing this will be. Why..."],["Paloma","Really... Vice Captain, didn't I already say before that she has changed?"],["Paloma","In this this one's eyes, it's no longer just about herself."],["Leopold","...!"],["Rosa","...Right."],["","When draping this combat suit over the shoulders, it doesn't need to be worn; it clings like a living thing, gradually enveloping the body."],["Rosa","I'm not alone... I don't need to sacrifice myself to save everything..."],["Rosa","Kaidan, Ada... Sylvie... When they brought me back from that world, I should have realized this..."],["Rosa","If it's just one person, nothing can truly be saved."],["","Since that night in White Maple, Rosa felt as if she had died."],["","Like every broken clock displaying the date of its death, Rosa once thought she would be forever trapped in that night."],["","Now, awakening from a long dream, the clock has started ticking again, and everything begins to move forward."],["","This feeling is like opening her eyes for the first time."],["","That world beyond the five senses, the world of arashi material that could only be sensed in a blur, is now displayed before her with unparalleled clarity."],["Rosa","Atonement, sacrifice—no, I do not fight for those things, but rather to believe... to believe that we will ultimately prevail."],["Rosa","And believe that no matter what I become, everyone will bring me straight back!"],["Rosa","So alongside you all—I will fight!"]],"561022101":[["","Reversion Paradox Incident\nParticipant Inquiry Record"],["Sloth","What the... Why start with me first..."],["Sloth","But before we start, can I ask about Rosa's condition first...? It affects whether I need to work overtime later..."],["Sloth","Stable? Trying new treatment methods... That's a relief."],["Sloth","Yeah... Morgana brought quite a few people over, and those Obsidian guys fought for a long time... How should I describe that scene..."],["Sloth","I guess... savage?"],["Sloth","A way of battle totally indifferent to destruction and death. Maybe I shouldn't call it fighting. What's a better word? Slaughter?"],["Sloth","But the result was good. Maybe Morgana had better reserves, or perhaps Rosa's previous blows to the enemy were strong enough... Anyway, we won."],["Sloth","What? You still want to ask about the details of the event? Let me be clear, it's not that I'm afraid of trouble, it's just that my memory isn't that good for these things..."],["Sloth","Just talk about the things you remember, huh... Let me think..."],["Sloth","Actually, when the Vice Captain insisted on sending me out to intercept, I felt something was off... He knows me well, and in that situation, staying at the base would definitely suit me better."],["Sloth","With him commanding on-site, Paloma definitely wouldn't be able to slip away midway... I dare say, no one would find an opportunity to leak."],["Sloth","As you know, a series of chaotic events occurred."],["Sloth","At times like this, what I can do is indeed limited, but since the Vice Captain didn't say anything, I also felt everything was under control... until I got shot in the battle..."],["Sloth","..."],["Sloth","Why do you think I did it? Hmm... how should I put it? I did regret it afterwards, but..."],["Sloth","When do you think people would sacrifice their lives for others?"],["Sloth","My answer is—to die for those who would die for me... quite a beautiful sentiment, isn't it?"],["Sloth","But beautiful words can't stop the pain... When Rosa asked me if I ever thought about dying, I was truly taken aback."],["Sloth","I still choose to believe in her... because that's the team's choice... This team is already my final destination. If it doesn't give up on me, I won't give up on it."],["Sloth","Although everyone has a lot hidden in their hearts... Unlike me, even if you go and ask them, they probably won't be honest."],["Sloth","But as long as you understand that everyone acts for others based on their own perceptions and positions, you'll realize that nothing has gone wrong."],["Sloth","You see, the Vice Captain really had a trick up his sleeve, one shot and he brought me back to life, not bad..."],["Sloth","...Anything else to add? I'm tired of talking, others surely have more to say... I'll just add one more thing..."],["Sloth","Captain, you really have a wonderful sister."],["Paloma","It's my turn, it's my turn... Huh? Am I the second one? I thought you'd save me for the finale?"],["Paloma","Sloth already told you what happened afterward, right? Rosa's condition was just discussed, and you still want to hear from me..."],["Paloma","When did I start to suspect that Sapi was a traitor?"],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","Honestly, Sapi is really unbelievably stupid... Even after setting up all these facilities, why did he have to come over and take a look at me..."],["Paloma","Yes, yes, it's the last scene in the surveillance footage, the enemy who escaped right from under my gun."],["Paloma","I realized something was wrong when that one chose to escape... After all, I understand better than anyone that Obsidian folks would never run away just to save their lives."],["Paloma","At that time, I was a bit anxious and called out to Sapi a few times using the communicator. After a while, she finally responded, and I knew something had happened..."],["Paloma","She probably used the excuse of the defense line being breached to switch to another ST, intending to find a secluded place to send coordinates. But what she didn't expect was that someone had triggered the alarm beforehand."],["Paloma","Why wasn't the switched ST recognized? Are you only noticing now that the spare STs and puppets used at that base are all Obsidian models?"],["Paloma","Anyway, since then I've known that Sapi was up to something sneaky... But I didn't plan to expose her, after all, she wasn't in the Southern City when the leak happened."],["Paloma","At that time, I thought I'd wait until all this was over and then teach her a lesson privately when we got back... But..."],["Paloma","That Rosa, she's really sharp. Even after guessing that Leopold leaked the information, she remained vigilant, seeking the truth."],["Paloma","I wanted to persuade her not to overthink, but who knew, Morgana sent that message back at that moment..."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","...Sorry..."],["Paloma","I've told you before, haven't I?"],["Paloma","Before I met Sapi, there was a long period when I lived like a zombie, eating, researching, sleeping, day in and day out..."],["Paloma","Everyone says research and discovering new things is so interesting, but to me, it's all just what it should be, and then you have to spend days, months, or years proving it... What's even more ridiculous is that quite a few people use these results as bargaining chips in their struggles."],["Paloma","This is boring, that's boring—I was so picky back then, living was harder than dying... What surprised me the most was that quite a few people envied my supposed talent."],["Paloma","If it were you, you would understand, right? This pain that ordinary people can't comprehend... Don't you? Sorry... I don't feel that way now, though..."],["Paloma","But just like a child being punished, locked in the closet by their parents for days, they can still amuse themselves by playing with their fingers in the light through the cabinet cracks. I was the same back then."],["Paloma","Even in painful circumstances, people can find joy... No, they must find joy; it's an instinct that cannot be suppressed."],["Paloma","So I did a lot of terrible things to myself, and everyone accused me of wasting my talent, saying I should cherish my body for my talent. But... Sapi was different; she saw me, not just my talent."],["Paloma","My life, perhaps it was given to me by Sapi at that time."],["Paloma","So at that time, I wanted to take the blame for the traitor for Sapi. I... I even thought about... sniping with an ST to kill Rosa to hide the truth..."],["Paloma","Even you... don't blame me?"],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","Really, I'm not crying... Besides, you're the least qualified to call me childish, aren't you?"],["Paloma","But fortunately, I didn't do it in the end... Maybe it also proves that I trusted Rosa at that time..."],["Paloma","Captain, Rosa is truly an amazing person... We'll bring her back."],["Veronica","Didn't I already let you go? Why are you still..."],["Veronica","Haha, I never thought it would be your turn to ask me questions... Go ahead, what do you want to know?"],["Veronica","Why help you? Let me be clear, I still oppose your plan to cooperate with Obsidian, it's just..."],["Veronica","If this is the only way to wake Rosa, then I won't interfere for now."],["Veronica","...!!"],["Veronica","Damn it, has Leopold already told you all about me? Didn't I tell him... never mind..."],["Veronica","In the past, I used to think that my purpose in life might be to kill Rosa one day, to give an explanation to those who died for me."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Of course, you can't understand. It's not easy for a person to find a purpose to live."],["Veronica","After surviving such a hell, I once thought that all the happiness in my remaining life would only be sin."],["Veronica","But after actually meeting Rosa, I increasingly don't understand what I should do... Her confession is sincere, but how should I bury everything I've been through?"],["Veronica","I quickly adjusted my mood... After dealing with the trouble of traitors and the like, I'll hand her over to the Oceanic Conclave for judgment."],["Veronica","But what I didn't expect was that even facing someone like me, she still chose to trust... So I..."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Damn, I don't even know how to describe it... In any case, forgiving her is not something I can do, but I will strive for a chance for her."],["Veronica","The only one who can forgive her is herself."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","Alright, alright, no need to say thank you or anything. I can't handle Captain Ada's gratitude... You know, someone has to be responsible for this."],["Veronica","I will take Sapientia to headquarters, but I'm not sure how much time the two of us can buy for you..."],["Veronica","By the way, can you pass a message to Rosa when she wakes up?"],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","I will try to live in her way."],["Veronica","No longer for redemption, but for... a better future."],["Sapientia","...!!"],["Sapientia","I-I'm sorry, I didn't notice earlier, I'll get up right away... Huh? I just need to keep lying down?"],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Yeah, Veronica already said that after I rest for a while, she'll take me back to headquarters to handle some affairs."],["Sapientia","It's not a big deal, really. At that time, Rosa blocked the last round of bombing, and then..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Rosa, indeed, did she fall unconscious again to save me..."],["Sapientia","No... don't comfort me... If it weren't for me, Obsidian might not have found that city..."],["Sapientia","I made a mistake and must bear the cost for it, that's beyond doubt."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Well... Allow me to explain the situation at that time..."],["Sapientia","I arranged the three STs to attract Paloma, as well as the nearby cameras. I hoped to create an alibi for her, who was closest to me."],["Sapientia","The breach in the defense line was intentional on my part... It was to ensure ample time to switch an ST, then find a location with no one around to send coordinates, and later find an opportunity to switch back to my own ST."],["Sapientia","But at that time, I was a bit worried and wanted to check if Paloma had run off. As a result, I got shot when she discovered me..."],["Sapientia","What? You say Paloma had already discovered my identity back then... Haha, she must have thought I was incredibly stupid, right?"],["Sapientia","Indeed, this level of planning is nowhere near the Vice Captain's. If I leaked the coordinates, it wouldn't take long for Rosa to find out."],["Sapientia","At that time, I had no idea what was happening. I just knew the alarm was sounding, and I had to hurry back to my ST..."],["Sapientia","Could it be a false alarm? Later, I even had this stupid thought... I really resist suspecting everyone, because apart from someone like me, no one would become a traitor..."],["Sapientia","It wasn't until Rosa asked me that question that I realized the traitor might be the Vice Captain... I'm sorry... At that moment, I was even a bit happy, because if it was the vice captain, he would definitely stop this mission properly..."],["Sapientia","To protect the Vice Captain, I lied... I lied to Rosa, relying on everyone's trust in me..."],["Sapientia","Everything that happened afterward was completely beyond my expectations, the arguments, the battles... This is not what I wanted to see..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Heh... Strange, isn't it? Even though I was thinking about sacrificing others for safety, I made that choice at that moment."],["Sapientia","But maybe, as Rosa said, I've already started to regret it."],["Sapientia","Afterwards, Paloma stood up for me... If I had a bit more courage, I wouldn't have put everyone in danger... But..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Captain, I believe the final assault doesn't truly represent the real strength of Obsidian headquarters... Although I've only seen the tip of the iceberg, the technology they possess now..."],["Sapientia","That's right, their imitation of Rebirth technology is, at best, nothing more than a form of entertainment."],["Sapientia","And then... not only do they possess power, but like the Vice Captain, they only take action when victory is assured."],["Sapientia","In their original plan, even at the risk of exposing my identity, I would provide them with coordinates, and troop deployment was adjusted based on this."],["Sapientia","If it weren't for the vice captain's plan or my premature exposure and control, they would have conducted a full-scale bombardment earlier or sent more soldiers. But in any case... time was indeed delayed."],["Sapientia","Without everyone, everything will... If I could..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Has Morgana already told you about this... Sorry, even now I'm still so useless..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Captain, can I return to this squad again... Really!? Thank you..."],["Sapientia","And then... if Rosa wakes up, I hope I can properly thank her again."],["Sapientia","She forgave me, and I must respond to her."],["Leopold","What? I thought you didn't want to hear me ramble anymore..."],["Leopold","Is it really time to start scheming against them? Hey, hey, don't make me sound like some old villain."],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","Listen, I've told Rosa this too, I've always believed in them... so I can't give them the chance to make mistakes."],["Leopold","Acting not out of suspicion, but out of trust, is the duty of a leader. You should learn from it."],["Leopold","...You say you knew all along? Fine, whatever I say, you'll just talk back."],["Leopold","At that time, according to my plan, each of them should have held a part of the clue, and starting as the initial leaker, it would be easy to deduce my suspicion..."],["Leopold","That's right, I'm looking for the liar."],["Leopold","If the other side noticed me, chances are they'd choose to cover for me. Is that what you'd call a leaker's unspoken pact?"],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","You mean Paloma? Haha, when she was slipping Rosa the medicine, I had already noticed... That one's terrible at hiding things."],["Leopold","Until Rosa exposed it in the end, I couldn't detect any obvious lies. No... if I had to say, Sapientia's final stance did make me suspicious, some terrible suspicions..."],["Leopold","Maybe she was the leaker, and at the last moment, she chose to push to ensure her innocence."],["Leopold","She might seek an opportunity to contact Obsidian after I was controlled... so I had to resist at that time, had to keep delaying."],["Leopold","Speaking of which, wasn't the whole point of the plan to buy time? We couldn't let the real leaker discover that the base's coordinates hadn't been exposed—everything was about dragging everyone into this game of deduction to delay the leak..."],["Leopold","Judging from the final result, it was a success."],["Leopold","Except for how Paloma stepped in at the end... Honestly, that was indeed unexpected for me, but... Fortunately, it seems she learned something this time and didn't cause any substantial damage."],["Leopold","Alright, is there anything you don't understand about this incident... Oh? You're asking me what I think of Rosa?"],["Leopold","..."],["Leopold","To be honest, in the past, I didn't want you to meet her again, but now..."],["Leopold","Ada, I'm glad she's your sister."],["","???"],["Paloma","Now, the captain's belongings might affect the arashi element within her... Try to control it within five minutes."],["","The visitor nodded, opened the door to the care room, and walked to the bedside."],["","She wanted to reach out and touch the face of the comatose person, but recalling Paloma's advice, her hand froze in mid-air, then regretfully withdrew."],["","After five minutes of silence, the visitor turned around, and before leaving, she finally gathered everything she wanted to convey."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Sister, everyone has told me about your situation..."],["Ada","I promise, we'll bring you back once more."]]};
